\"url\":\"https://www.cato.org/commentary/economic-leadership-secrets-benito-mussolini\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"27\",\"title\":\"The Great Depression and U.S. Foreign Policy - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The U.S. stock market crash of 1929, an economic downturn in Germany, and financial difficulties in France and Great Britain all coincided to cause a global ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1921-1936/great-depression\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"28\",\"title\":\"Hannah Arendt - Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy\",\"description\":\"Jul 27, 2006 · Thus, totalitarianism is based on a secular, pseudo-scientific ideology that reduces the complexity of reality to the logic of one idea ...\",\"url\":\"https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/arendt/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"29\",\"title\":\"The Rise of Fascism | History of Western Civilization II\",\"description\":\"After Fascism's accommodation of the political right, the Fascist movement's membership soared to approximately 250,000 by 1921. Fascists Seize Power. Beginning ...\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/suny-hccc-worldhistory2/chapter/the-rise-of-fascism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"30\",\"title\":\"Timeline: important events of Mussolini - Timetoast\",\"description\":\"Birth of Mussolini. Jul 29, 1883 · Fascist party founded. May 29, 1919 · Advertisements · Leads Blackshirts on Rome to Seize Power. Oct 27, 1922 · Hitler Meets With ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.timetoast.com/timelines/important-events-of-mussolini\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"31\",\"title\":\"A Chronology of the Rise of Italian Fascism\",\"description\":\"Fascists in Bologna reject Pact of Pacification and Mussolini resigns, not accepted by Grand Council of Fascism. Sept 12. Squads carry out \\\"punitive ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.sas.upenn.edu/~mercerb/chitfasc.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"32\",\"title\":\"Early development of the Nazi Party, 1920-1922 - Hitler's rise ... - BBC\",\"description\":\"1920 – The group changed its name to the National Socialist German Workers Party (NSDAP) – or Nazis for short. 1921 – Hitler was elected Party Chairman and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/guides/z3bp82p/revision/1\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"33\",\"title\":\"Adolf Hitler and the Nazi Rise to Power, 1918–1933\",\"description\":\"Jun 23, 2025 · Nazi Party leader Adolf Hitler became chancellor of Germany on January 30, 1933. In the months that followed, the Nazis transformed Germany from a democracy ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/the-nazi-rise-to-power\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"34\",\"title\":\"How Did Adolf Hitler Happen? | The National WWII Museum\",\"description\":\"Adolf Hitler was appointed chancellor of Germany in 1933 following a series of electoral victories by the Nazi Party. Learn more about his rise to power.The Invasion of Poland · From War to War in Europe · The Holocaust\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/how-did-adolf-hitler-happen\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"35\",\"title\":\"Hitler Comes to Power: How, When, \u0026 Key Dates\",\"description\":\"Sep 23, 2025 · The full name of the Nazi Party was the National Socialist German Workers' Party. Its members were often called Nazis. The Nazis were radically ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/hitler-comes-to-power\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"36\",\"title\":\"Hitler becomes dictator of Germany | August 2, 1934 - History.com\",\"description\":\"... of Hitler's Bavarian-based Nazi party swelled with resentful Germans. A paramilitary organization, the Sturmabteilung (SA), was formed to protect the Nazis and ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/august-2/hitler-becomes-fuhrer\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"37\",\"title\":\"Joseph Stalin - Soviet Leader, Dictator, Purges | Britannica\",\"description\":\"Sep 23, 2025 · By 1937, after less than a decade's rule as totalitarian dictator, he had increased the Soviet Union's total industrial output to the point ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Joseph-Stalin/Legacy\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"38\",\"title\":\"Internal Workings of the Soviet Union - Revelations from the Russian ...\",\"description\":\"Stalin's “revolution from above” sought to build socialism by means of forced collectivization and industrialization, programs that entailed tremendous human ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.loc.gov/exhibits/archives/intn.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"39\",\"title\":\"Great Purge | History \u0026 Facts - Britannica\",\"description\":\"Sep 20, 2025 · Stalin industrialized the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics, forcibly collectivized its agriculture, consolidated his position by intensive ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/Great-Purge\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"40\",\"title\":\"Stalin's Soviet Union: The Archetype of Totalitarianism\",\"description\":\"Nov 2, 2022 · One of the central aspects of Stalin's rule was his drive for rapid industrialization, which was implemented through a series of Five-Year Plans ...\",\"url\":\"https://sociology.institute/political-sociology/stalins-soviet-union-totalitarianism-archetype/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"41\",\"title\":\"Japan - Militarism, Imperialism, WWII | Britannica\",\"description\":\"The notion that expansion through military conquest would solve Japan's economic problems gained currency during the Great Depression of the 1930s.\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/place/Japan/The-rise-of-the-militarists\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"42\",\"title\":\"Authoritarianism in Japan (article) | Khan Academy\",\"description\":\"Militarism and the rise of the fascist imperialism ... By 1930, Japanese leaders saw themselves as facing two potential enemies. One was the young Soviet Union.\",\"url\":\"https://www.khanacademy.org/humanities/world-history-project-ap/xb41992e0ff5e0f09:unit-7-global-conflict/xb41992e0ff5e0f09:unresolved-tensions-after-world-war-i-7-5/a/article-authoritarianism-in-japan-ap\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"43\",\"title\":\"Japan's March Toward Militarism - Bill Gordon\",\"description\":\"Japanese militarism and imperialism steadily developed for five principal reasons. ... rise to an expansion of militarism and imperialism from 1905 to the 1930s.\",\"url\":\"http://www.bill-gordon.net/papers/jhist2.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"44\",\"title\":\"[PDF] 12 Japanese imperialism, 1930–1945 | Cambridge Core\",\"description\":\"So for both domestic and foreign reasons, the shift toward liberalism and informal imperialism in the 1920s was reversed in the 1930s. Reform bureau- crats and ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://resolve.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/6214BE406207D2E29703B60910265CD4/9781139236751c12_p371-397_CBO.pdf/japanese_imperialism_19301945.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"45\",\"title\":\"How Britain Hoped To Avoid War With Germany In The 1930s | IWM\",\"description\":\"Appeasement has come to be a byword for weakness and its failure to avoid war in the 1930s has been invoked as a reason to avoid resorting to it since then.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/how-britain-hoped-to-avoid-war-with-germany-in-the-1930s\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"46\",\"title\":\"Appeasement and 'Peace for Our Time' | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Oct 15, 2024 · Neville Chamberlain did not live long after the collapse of his appeasement policy ... Although his efforts failed to prevent war, even ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/appeasement-and-peace-our-time\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"47\",\"title\":\"The British Policy of Appeasement toward Hitler and Nazi Germany\",\"description\":\"The Failure of the Munich Agreement and the End of Appeasement. Link copied. The Munich Agreement failed to stop Nazi Germany's territorial aggression. In March ...\",\"url