and the Locarno Treaty.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyfromonestudenttoanother.com/as-level-international-history-1870-1945/the-league-of-nations-and-international-relations-in-the-1930s/why-did-britain-and-france-pursue-a-policy-of-appeasement/1936-remilitarisation-of-the-rhineland\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"54\",\"title\":\"1938: Anschluss with Austria - History: From One Student to Another\",\"description\":\"Many in the British public supported the policy of appeasement, therefore they were in no position to fight against German-Austrian unification.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyfromonestudenttoanother.com/as-level-international-history-1870-1945/the-league-of-nations-and-international-relations-in-the-1930s/why-did-britain-and-france-pursue-a-policy-of-appeasement/1938-anschluss-with-austria-1938\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"55\",\"title\":\"Munich Pact signed | September 30, 1938 - History.com\",\"description\":\"Jul 21, 2010 · The agreement averted the outbreak of war but gave Czechoslovakia away to German conquest. In the spring of 1938, Hitler began openly to support ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/september-30/munich-pact-signed\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"56\",\"title\":\"Munich Agreement | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"The leaders of Britain, France, and Italy agreed to the German annexation of the Sudetenland in exchange for a pledge of peace from Hitler. Czechoslovakia, ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/timeline-event/holocaust/1933-1938/munich-agreement\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"57\",\"title\":\"German-Soviet Nonaggression Pact | History, Facts, \u0026 Significance\",\"description\":\"German-Soviet Nonaggression Pact, pact signed on August 23, 1939, between Germany and the Soviet Union that was concluded a few days before the beginning of ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/German-Soviet-Nonaggression-Pact\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"58\",\"title\":\"German-Soviet Pact | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Sep 7, 2023 · The German-Soviet Pact was signed in August 1939. It paved the way for Nazi Germany and the Soviet Union to invade and occupy Poland that September.\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/german-soviet-pact\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"59\",\"title\":\"Invasion of Poland, Fall 1939 | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Aug 25, 2021 · In all, Germany deployed 60 divisions and nearly 1.5 million men in the invasion. From East Prussia and Germany in the north, and Silesia and ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/invasion-of-poland-fall-1939\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"60\",\"title\":\"The Invasion of Poland - The National WWII Museum\",\"description\":\"Oct 17, 2023 · By the morning of September 1, 1939, Hitler was already using the Gleiwitz incident to justify his invasion of Poland. The attack at ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/invasion-poland-september-1939\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"61\",\"title\":\"Germany invades Poland | September 1, 1939 - History.com\",\"description\":\"... invasion with overwhelming numbers of troops, tanks and artillery. ... Polish soldiers captured by the Germans during invasion of Poland, September 1939.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/september-1/germany-invades-poland\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"62\",\"title\":\"Soviet Union invades Poland | September 17, 1939 - History.com\",\"description\":\"Battle of Antietam breaks out. The Battle of Antietam was a pivotal, bloody Civil War skirmish on September 17, 1862, that halted Confederate momentum on the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/september-17/soviet-union-invades-poland\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"63\",\"title\":\"Invasion from the East - Warfare History Network\",\"description\":\"After signing a secret non-aggression pact with Nazi Germany, the Soviet Union invaded neighboring Poland in the early days of World War II.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/soviet-invasion-of-poland/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"64\",\"title\":\"Britain and France declare war on Germany | September 3, 1939\",\"description\":\"On September 3, 1939, in response to Hitler's invasion of Poland, Britain and France, both allies of the overrun nation declare war on Germany.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/september-3/britain-and-france-declare-war-on-germany\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"65\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Soviet Decision for War against Finland, 30 November 1939\",\"description\":\"Comparable demands were made to Finland at the beginning of October yet in spite of three visits to Moscow from 10 October to 13 November by the Finnish ...\",\"url\":\"https://sites.evergreen.edu/russiawinter/wp-content/uploads/sites/47/2015/01/Feb-10-SovWarAgainstFinland.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"66\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Winter War: Its Causes and Effects - DigitalCommons@Cedarville\",\"description\":\"Apr 4, 2018 · 13—Finland's high casualties forced it to sign a peace treaty giving in to Russian demands.58. Though in theory the war ended in a Russian ...Missing:  \\\"historical | Show results with:\\\"historical\",\"url\":\"https://digitalcommons.cedarville.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1037\u0026context=channels\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"67\",\"title\":\"Drifting towards war\",\"description\":\"The terms of the Moscow Peace Treaty were hard for Finland. Finland was forced to cede a part of the Karelian Isthmus, including the cities of Vyborg, Sortavala ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.defmin.fi/winterwar/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"68\",\"title\":\"The Winter War | Air \u0026 Space Forces Magazine\",\"description\":\"Sep 1, 2012 · The Winter War cost Finland 68,480 casualties, including 24,923 dead or missing, and 43,557 wounded.\",\"url\":\"https://www.airandspaceforces.com/article/0912f