wing the force to seize Dieppe and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/operation-jubilee-dieppe-raid-1942\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"133\",\"title\":\"World War II: D-Day, The Invasion of Normandy\",\"description\":\"Casualties from these countries during the landing numbered 10,300. By June 30, over 850,000 men, 148,000 vehicles, and 570,000 tons of supplies had landed on ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.eisenhowerlibrary.gov/research/online-documents/world-war-ii-d-day-invasion-normandy\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"134\",\"title\":\"Timeline of Pacific War - The History Place\",\"description\":\"December 7, 1941 - Japanese bomb Pearl Harbor, Hawaii; also attack the Philippines, Wake Island, Guam, Malaya, Thailand, Shanghai and Midway.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyplace.com/unitedstates/pacificwar/timeline.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"135\",\"title\":\"The Pacific Strategy, 1941-1944 | The National WWII Museum\",\"description\":\"On December 7, 1941, Japan staged a surprise attack on Pearl Harbor, severely damaging the US Pacific Fleet. When Germany and Italy declared war on the ...Missing:  casualties | Show results with:casualties\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/pacific-strategy-1941-1944\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"136\",\"title\":\"The Battle of Midway | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"The Battle of Midway was a key battle to secure dominance in the Pacific in World War II. Learn more about the strategies employed during this battle.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/battle-midway\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"137\",\"title\":\"History - U.S. Marine Corps Forces, Pacific\",\"description\":\"Over the seven months of the Guadalcanal campaign, U.S. forces took startlingly high casualties, with 7,100 dead and almost 8,000 wounded.Missing:  details | Show results with:details\",\"url\":\"https://www.marforpac.marines.mil/Unit-Home/History/Pacific-Campaig