ure the island, was ferocious, and resulted in 49,151 American casualties.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/browse-by-topic/wars-conflicts-and-operations/world-war-ii/1945/battle-of-okinawa.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"143\",\"title\":\"The Atomic Bombing of Hiroshima and Nagasaki\",\"description\":\"On August 6, 1945, at approximately 8:15 am locally, the B-29 bomber Enola Gay dropped the atomic bomb “Little Boy” on the Japanese city of Hiroshima.Missing:  effects | Show results with:effects\",\"url\":\"https://visit.archives.gov/whats-on/explore-exhibits/atomic-bombing-hiroshima-and-nagasaki\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"144\",\"title\":\"Japan's Surrender and Aftermath\",\"description\":\"The successful U.S. invasions of Iwo Jima in February and Okinawa in April had brought the Pacific War to the Japanese Home Islands' doorsteps. Devastating air ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/browse-by-topic/wars-conflicts-and-operations/world-war-ii/1945/victory-in-pacific.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"145\",\"title\":\"Atomic Salvation: How the A-Bomb Saved the Lives of 32 Million ...\",\"description\":\"Jan 5, 2021 · Lewis estimates that the bombing of Hiroshima and Nagasaki, to the extent that it induced Japanese surrender, saved the lives of roughly 30 million people.\",\"url\":\"https://www.airuniversity.af.edu/AUPress/Book-Reviews/Display/Article/2462838/atomic-salvation-how-the-a-bomb-saved-the-lives-of-32-million-people/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"146\",\"title\":\"World War II in the Pacific | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Jul 15, 2025 · More than 250,000 Americans were wounded in the Pacific theater. More than 100,000 US service members died while fighting against Imperial Japan ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/world-war-ii-in-the-pacific\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"147\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.usmm.org/battleatlantic.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"148\",\"title\":\"Battle of the Atlantic - Naval History and Heritage Command\",\"description\":\"Jan 12, 2021 · The Germans lost 783 U-boats and approximately 30,000 sailors, three quarters of Germany's 40,000-man submarine force. For a closer examination ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/browse-by-topic/wars-conflicts-and-operations/world-war-ii/1942/atlantic.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"149\",\"title\":\"H-019-4 \\\"Black May\\\": Battle of the Atlantic 1943\",\"description\":\"The peak of pitched Atlantic convoy battles occurred in March 1943, when U-boats sank 567,000 tons of Allied shipping. (Note that statistics in the Battle of ...Missing:  tonnage | Show results with:tonnage\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/about-us/leadership/director/directors-corner/h-grams/h-gram-019/h-019-4.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"150\",\"title\":\"The Battle That Had to Be Won | Naval History Magazine\",\"description\":\"The tide of the struggle between German U-boats and Allied convoy escorts shifted back and forth before definitively turning in the spring of 1943.\",\"url\":\"https://www.usni.org/magazines/naval-history-magazine/2008/june/battle-had-be-won\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"151\",\"title\":\"The Key Role of the Convoys | Naval History Magazine\",\"description\":\"Transporting supplies and soldiers in convoys protected by escorts using emerging antisubmarine technologies was crucial to the Allies sustaining Britain.Missing:  developments | Show results with:developments\",\"url\":\"https://www.usni.org/magazines/naval-history-magazine/2020/august/key-role-convoys\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"152\",\"title\":\"The Battle of the Atlantic explained | Imperial War Museums\",\"description\":\"The Battle of the Atlantic pitted Allied convoys protecting supply ships from North America and the Empire against German submarines (U-boats) and warships.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/the-battle-of-the-atlantic-explained\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"153\",\"title\":\"Supplying Victory: The History of Merchant Marine in World War II\",\"description\":\"Feb 7, 2022 · The US Merchant Marine provided crucial, yet often overlooked, logistical support for the Allied war effort.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/merchant-marine-world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"154\",\"title\":\"The American Economy during World War II – EH.net\",\"description\":\"WWII ended the depression, made the government a potent economic actor, revitalized industry, and increased personal income and quality of life.\",\"url\":\"https://eh.net/encyclopedia/the-american-economy-during-world-war-ii/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"155\",\"title\":\"Induction Statistics : Selective Service System\",\"description\":\"The following shows the number of men who were inducted into military service through the Selective Service System during the major 20th century conflicts.\",\"url\":\"https://www.sss.gov/history-and-records/induction-statistics/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"156\",\"title\":\"The Workers That Kept Britain Going During The Second World War\",\"description\":\"Minister of Labour Ernest Bevin was responsible for Britain's manpower resources. He introduced the Essential Work Order (EWO) which became law in March 1941.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/the-workers-that-kept-britain-going-during-the-second-world-war\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"157\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Resource mobilization for World War II: the U.S.A., U.K., U.S.S.R. ...\",\"description\":\"After 1940 German munitions production rose only slowly whereas Allied production ... the industrial economy (U.S. War Production Board: Washington, D.C., 1945).\",\"url\":\"https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/soc/economics/staff/mharrison/public/ehr88postprint.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"158\",\"title\":\"Wartime Evacuation - Seventeen Moments in Soviet History\",\"description\":\"A major goal of the evacuation effort was to defend and develop the Soviet military capability, so defense workers and factories were evacuated with the highest ...\",\"url\":\"https://soviethistory.msu.edu/1943-2/wartime-evacuation/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"159\",\"title\":\"Lend-Lease and Military Aid to the Allies in the Early Years of World ...\",\"description\":\"Over the course of the war, the United States contracted Lend-Lease agreements with more than 30 countries, dispensing some $50 billion in assistance.\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1937-1945/lend-lease\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"160\",\"title\":\"Lend-Lease to the Eastern Front | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Jul 29, 2024 · After the Germans initiated Operation Barbarossa in June 1941, the act was then applied to the Soviet Union, though initially on a paying basis.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/lend-lease-eastern-front\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"161\",\"title\":\"Axis Powers in World War II - Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Apr 22, 2022 · The three principal partners in the Axis alliance were Germany, Italy, and Japan. Learn more about the Axis powers in WW2.\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/axis-powers-in-world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"162\",\"title\":\"The Axis (Chapter 1) - The Cambridge History of the Second World ...\",\"description\":\"Once they embarked on the path to total war, Japan became a military dictatorship, while the power in Nazi Germany and Fascist Italy always remained firmly in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/cambridge-history-of-the-second-world-war/axis/15C668DE63B50F10EF50673B0118116E\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"163\",\"title\":\"Axis Powers: The Infamous Tripartite Pact - Warfare History Network\",\"description\":\"Axis Powers: The Infamous Tripartite Pact. Imperial Japan joined Nazi Germany and Fascist Italy in World War II to engage Great Britain and the United States.Japan's Decision To Join The... · Germany Prepares For A Long... · Attack On Pearl HarborMissing:  internal relations\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/axis-powers-the-infamous-tripartite-pact/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"164\",\"title\":\"6 reasons why Fascist Italy underperformed during World War II\",\"description\":\"Aug 9, 2022 · Italy failed to achieve much of what it tried to do and the great victories by Italian troops often came under the direction of German leadership.\",\"url\":\"https://www.wearethemighty.com/articles/6-reasons-why-fascist-italy-underperformed-during-world-war-ii/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"165\",\"title\":\"Seven Reasons Why the Italian Forces Performed So Poorly During ...\",\"description\":\"Aug 12, 2022 · The Italians had outdated and minimal weaponry · Italian industry wasn't prepared for war · The Italian Army was made up of poorly-trained troops.\",\"url\":\"https://www.warhistoryonline.com/world-war-ii/italy-wwii.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"166\",\"title\":\"SPE Delta Section: A Study of the Role of Oil in World War II and Its ...\",\"description\":\"Feb 1, 2025 · Prior to the war, Germany consumed about 110 KBOPD. 80% of that supply was lost at the start of hostilities (Fig. 4).\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://jpt.spe.org/spe-delta-section-a-study-of-the-role-of-oil-in-world-war-ii-and-its-strategic-impact\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"167\",\"title\":\"Oil and War: ten conclusions from WWII? - Thunder Said Energy\",\"description\":\"Mar 3, 2022 · General US oil rationing provoked outrage. Interestingly, it was motivated just as much by rubber shortages as oil shortages. Japan's ...\",\"url\":\"https://thundersaidenergy.com/2022/03/03/oil-and-war-ten-conclusions-from-wwii/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"168\",\"title\":\"The German synthetic fuel effort: Origins, development, and legacy\",\"description\":\"May 15, 2025 · Germany began researching synthetic fuels after WWI due to lack of oil,