rol of 90% of the world's natural rubber during World War II, the US allies never suffered from a shortage ...\",\"url\":\"https://defense.info/re-thinking-strategy/2018/10/oil-and-war/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"174\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Road to Total War: 00D Escalation in World War II - DTIC\",\"description\":\"Aug 13, 2025 · The escalation of WWII had no single cause, resulting from various factors, including Germany's attacks on London and the British shift to ...\",\"url\":\"https://apps.dtic.mil/sti/tr/pdf/AD0688212.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"175\",\"title\":\"Immeasurable Brutality, the Nazi–Soviet War 1941–1945\",\"description\":\"Jun 19, 2024 · It is an opportune time to reexamine the immeasurably brutal war between Nazi Germany and the Soviet Union.Missing:  sources | Show results with:sources\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/immeasurable-brutality-nazi-soviet-war-1941-1945-interview-jeff-rutherford-phd\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"176\",\"title\":\"Propaganda Experts, Intelligence, and Total War (1941–1945) | KNOW\",\"description\":\"This article investigates the entangled history of the propaganda battles waged during World War II, focusing on Germany, the Soviet Union, and the United ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/10.1086/710328\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"177\",\"title\":\"Ideologies (Part I) - The Cambridge History of the Second World War\",\"description\":\"By the time he came out of prison, Hitler had assembled the ideology of Nazism from disparate elements of anti-Semitism, pan-Germanism, eugenics and so-called ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/cambridge-history-of-the-second-world-war/ideologies/6CC660D69D3105B8BE68749D9C22F41A\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"178\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Nazi Ideology and the Pursuit of War Aim: 1941-45\",\"description\":\"The following sources will aid this thesis in examining questions which have plagued historians since the conclusion of World War II. This thesis will rely ...\",\"url\":\"https://digitalcommons.georgiasouthern.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=2255\u0026context=etd\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"179\",\"title\":\"Nazi Policy on the Eastern Front, 1941: Total War, Genocide, and ...\",\"description\":\"The ruthless ideological war waged by the Nazi state against the Soviet Union manifested itself in a myriad of ways, from the German army's murder of Red Army ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/10.7722/j.ctt81f64\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"180\",\"title\":\"Japan's Imperial Ambitions: Unpacking the Ideologies, Propaganda ...\",\"description\":\"Feb 24, 2025 · Propaganda was a tool for the Japanese government to control the narrative and present its imperial ventures in a patriotic light. To ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.pacificatrocities.org/blog/japans-imperial-ambitions-unpacking-the-ideologies-propaganda-and-human-cost-of-empire-in-manchuria\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"181\",\"title\":\"Visual Puppeteer: Japanese Propaganda During World War II\",\"description\":\"Jan 10, 2019 · Propaganda was used either as a mechanism to heighten a sense of nationalism or as a weapon to demonize and dehumanize enemies.\",\"url\":\"https://www.pacificatrocities.org/blog/visual-puppeteer-japanese-propaganda-during-world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"182\",\"title\":\"Propaganda from World War II - Primary Sources\",\"description\":\"The Axis powers, particularly Nazi Germany, utilized propaganda to promote the ideology of Aryan supremacy, justify their expansionist policies, and dehumanize ...Missing:  methods | Show results with:methods\",\"url\":\"https://libguides.fau.edu/primary-sources-ww2/propaganda\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"183\",\"title\":\"World War II Propaganda | American Experience | Official Site - PBS\",\"description\":\"Goebbels promoted the Nazi message through art, music, theater, films, books, radio, and the press, and censored all opposition.\",\"url\":\"https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/americanexperience/features/goebbels-propaganda/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"184\",\"title\":\"Japanese PSYOP During WWII - Psywarrior\",\"description\":\"During World War II, numerous propaganda leaflets were produced by the Japanese military and distributed from airplanes to the Asian populace and enemy troops.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.psywarrior.com/JapanPSYOPWW2.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"185\",\"title\":\"Powers of Persuasion | National Archives\",\"description\":\"Jun 6, 2019 · It explores the strategies of persuasion as evidenced in the form and content of World War II posters.\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/exhibits/powers-of-persuasion\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"186\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.org.uk/files/download/499/1204285703/stalin_propaganda.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"187\",\"title\":\"Rosie the Riveter and Benny the Bungler: WWII Propaganda at Work\",\"description\":\"May 16, 2020 · They used psychological tactics, guilt, and emotions to appeal to the patriotism and loyalty of the public. Posters addressed things like safety ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/wwii-propaganda\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"188\",\"title\":\"The Power of Propaganda in World War II - Nelson University\",\"description\":\"Aug 29, 2018 · The answer-propaganda and lots of it. While propaganda took many forms, perhaps its strongest and the most effective channel was Hollywood films.Missing:  methods | Show results with:methods\",\"url\":\"https://www.nelson.edu/thoughthub/communication/the-power-of-propaganda-in-world-war-ii/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"189\",\"title\":\"Tank Clash – The German Panther vs. the Soviet T-34-85\",\"description\":\"Mar 20, 2015 · On the battlefield, the Panther was formidable; its broad tracks distributed the tanks weight evenly allowing the 44-ton machine to traverse ...\",\"url\":\"https://militaryhistorynow.com/2015/03/20/tank-clash-the-german-panther-vs-the-soviet-t-34-85/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"190\",\"title\":\"Innovating for Victory | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Inventions like synthetic rubber, the jeep, the atomic bomb, and even duct tape helped the Allies win World War II by allowing their militaries to wage war on ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/innovating-victory\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"191\",\"title\":\"Messerschmitt Me 262A Schwalbe - Air Force Museum\",\"description\":\"Developed from a 1938 design by the Messerschmitt company, the Me 262 Schwalbe was the world's first operational turbojet aircraft.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalmuseum.af.mil/Visit/Museum-Exhibits/Fact-Sheets/Display/Article/196266/messerschmitt-me-262a-schwalbe/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"192\",\"title\":\"V-2 Rocket - Air Force Museum\",\"description\":\"The V-2 was a powerful WWII German rocket with a 220-mile range, 3,400 mph speed, and used high-speed pumps. It was the most powerful rocket up to that time.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalmuseum.af.mil/Visit/Museum-Exhibits/Fact-Sheets/Display/Article/195894/v-2-rocket/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"193\",\"title\":\"Timeline - Manhattan Project National Historical Park (U.S. National ...\",\"description\":\"Officially lasting from June 18, 1942 to August 25, 1947, the Manhattan Project employed over 130,000 people throughout the United States.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nps.gov/mapr/learn/historyculture/timeline.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"194\",\"title\":\"U.S. Army History: Red Ball Express - Transportation Corps\",\"description\":\"The huge convoy stretching from horizon to horizon was part of the Red Ball Express, the famed trucking operation in the European Theater of Operations (ETO) in ...Keep 'em Rolling\\\" · On the Road to Victory · The Red Ball Express\",\"url\":\"https://transportation.army.mil/history/studies/red_ball_express.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"195\",\"title\":\"The Red Ball Express - Army University Press\",\"description\":\"The Red Ball Express route was a one-way highway that was only open to its drivers. To prevent confusion, all vehicles on the route had to be clearly marked ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.armyupress.army.mil/Journals/Military-Review/English-Edition-Archives/March-April-2021/Carey-Red-Ball-Express/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"196\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Historical Impact of Revealing The Ultra Secret\",\"description\":\"Oct 26, 2006 · Jn March of 1943, Ultra yielded a German code word recognized as signifying a shift to an additional (fourth) rotor within the Enigma machine ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nsa.gov/portals/75/documents/news-features/declassified-documents/cryptologic-spectrum/ultra_secret.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"197\",\"title\":\"War of Secrets: Cryptology in WWII - Air Force Museum\",\"description\":\"Breaking German and Japanese codes gave the Allies an important advantage in WWII -- it saved many lives and shortened the war, by some estimates as much as ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalmuseum.af.mil/Visit/Museum-Exhibits/Fact-Sheets/Display/Article/196193/war-of-secrets-cryptology-in-wwii/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"198\",\"title\":\"The Polish cryptographers who cracked the Enigma code\",\"description\":\"In 1932, Ciężki hired these students to join the bureau. They were Marian Rejewski, Jerzy Różycki and Henryk Zygalski, and their contribution would prove ...Missing:  breakthrough | Show results with:breakthrough\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.co.uk/articles/the-polish-cryptographers-who-cracked-the-enigma-code\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"199\",\"title\":\"How codebreakers helped fight the Battle of Britain - GCHQ.GOV.UK\",\"description\":\"Sep 15, 2020 · Analysts at GCHQ's forerunner Bletchley Park provided vital intelligence in the struggle to defend Britain's skies.\",\"url\":\"https://www.gchq.gov.uk/information/how-codebreakers-helped-fight-battle-britain\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"200\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Alan Turing, Enigma, and the Breaking of German Machine Ciphers ...\",\"description\":\"The intelligence reports based upon the breaking of the Ger- man Ciphers by these machines were referred to as \\\"Ultra intelligence. ... Bletchley Park). In this ...Missing:  impact | Show results with:impact\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/files/publications/prologue/1997/fall/turing.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"201\",\"title\":\"The Turing-Welchman Bombe - The National Museum of Computing\",\"description\":\"The Turing-Welchman Bombe machine was an electro-mechanical device used to break Enigma-enciphered messages about enemy military operations during the Second ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.tnmoc.org/bombe\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"202\",\"title\":\"[PDF] ULTRA: Its Operational Use in the European Theater of ... - DTIC\",\"description\":\"Within Bletchley Park, the actual \\\"codebreaking\\\" of the. German ENIGMA machine cyphers as well as other high level. (high security) cryptographic systems was ...\",\"url\":\"https://apps.dtic.mil/sti/tr/pdf/ADA234706.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"203\",\"title\":\"The Magic of Purple - National Security Agency\",\"description\":\"Aug 4, 2021 · The stunning success of Purple distracted the U.S. cryptologic community from the true indicator of Japanese intentions, the naval code.Missing:  WWII | Show results with:WWII\",\"url\":\"https://www.nsa.gov/History/National-Cryptologic-Museum/Exhibits-Artifacts/Exhibit-View/Article/2718925/the-magic-of-purple/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"204\",\"title\":\"How Roosevelt Attacked Japan at Pearl Harbor | National Archives\",\"description\":\"\\\"Magic\\\" provided intelligence of value to the State Department in formulating policy, but the military and naval threat to American territory posed by Japan ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/publications/prologue/1996/fall/butow.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"205\",\"title\":\"Red and Purple - National Security Agency\",\"description\":\"PURPLE was used for communication with major diplomatic posts -- Washington, London and Moscow, among others --- and RED for less important locations. Some ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nsa.gov/History/Cryptologic-History/Historical-Events/Article-View/Article/2740690/red-and-purple/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"206\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Intelligence during World War ZI: - GovInfo\",\"description\":\"No. UNITED STATES CRYPTOLOGIC HISTORY. A History of U.S. Communications. Intelligence during World War ... war began, the following numhrs of Japanese army ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-D-PURL-gpo52785/pdf/GOVPUB-D-PURL-gpo52785.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"207\",\"title\":\"World War II | MI5 - The Security Service\",\"description\":\"This was the famous \\\"Double Cross\\\" system, a highly ... Why MI5 was founded; the fight against German espionage; how MI5 caught German spy Carl Hans Lody.\",\"url\":\"https://www.mi5.gov.uk/history/world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"208\",\"title\":\"MI5 in world War II | MI5 - The Security Service\",\"description\":\"Its main wartime success was taking the lead role in the now celebrated 'Double Cross System', which fed disinformation to Germany through turned German agents.\",\"url\":\"https://www.mi5.gov.uk/history/world-war-ii/mi5-in-world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"209\",\"title\":\"D-Day Deception: Operation Fortitude South | English Heritage\",\"description\":\"The aim of the deception was to reinforce the belief among those in the German high command that the main Allied landings would be in the Pas-de-Calais, across ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/dover-castle/history-and-stories/d-day-deception/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"210\",\"title\":\"D-Day's Parachuting Dummies and Inflatable Tanks\",\"description\":\"The D-Day deception plan was codenamed Operation 'Fortitude' and was part of a larger overall deception strategy – Operation 'Bodyguard'.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/d-days-parachuting-dummies-and-inflatable-tanks\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"211\",\"title\":\"German Espionage and Sabotage\",\"description\":\"After Pearl Harbor, German espionage against the United States failed to produce the information required by the High Command.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/research/library/online-reading-room/title-list-alphabetically/g/german-espionage-and-sabotage.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"212\",\"title\":\"Admiral Canaris: Hitler's Slippery Spymaster\",\"description\":\"Sep 16, 2024 · Hitler's opinion of Canaris would continue to deteriorate as the war went on and Canaris continued to make intelligence “mistakes.” He ...\",\"url\":\"https://cimsec.org/admiral-canaris-hitlers-slippery-spymaster/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"213\",\"title\":\"Cold Conflict | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"One of the most critical Soviet spies was Klaus Fuchs, a leading physicist who worked on the Manhattan Project and was a member of the Communist Party. After ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/cold-conflict\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"214\",\"title\":\"Medical Innovations: Antibiotics | The National WWII Museum\",\"description\":\"Apr 27, 2020 · The plan identified 4 main steps to solving the problem: 1) Finding a strain of the fungus that produced a higher quantity of penicillin; 2) ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/medical-innovations-antibiotics\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"215\",\"title\":\"Penicillin: Opening the Era of Antibiotics - USDA ARS\",\"description\":\"Feb 8, 2024 · Large-scale commercial production of penicillin during the 1940s opened the era of antibiotics and is recognized as one of the great advances in civilization.\",\"url\":\"https://www.ars.usda.gov/midwest-area/peoria-il/national-center-for-agricultural-utilization-research/docs/penicillin-opening-the-era-of-antibiotics/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"216\",\"title\":\"Medical Innovations: Charles Drew and Blood Banking | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"May 4, 2020 · Drew developed a system to turn the blood into plasma, bottled into 1 liter units, and boxed six to a case for transport. In the end the program ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/medical-innovations-blood-banking\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"217\",\"title\":\"The military use of blood plasma as a substitute for wholeblood in ...\",\"description\":\"The clinical use of plasma forshock and hemorrhage was a development of World War II, just as the concept ofhemorrhagic shock was a development of that war.\",\"url\":\"https://achh.army.mil/history/book-wwii-blood-chapter11/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"218\",\"title\":\"Advances in Medicine During Wars - Foreign Policy Research Institute\",\"description\":\"Feb 23, 2018 · World War II saw the expanded use of antibiotics as a very significant advance. Sulfa drugs, discovered in 1935, and penicillin, developed ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.fpri.org/article/2018/02/advances-in-medicine-during-wars/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"219\",\"title\":\"Mulberry Harbors: The Allied Secret Weapon at Normandy\",\"description\":\"The artificial Mulberry harbors allowed supplies and reinforcements to come ashore directly on the beaches after the D-Day invasion.\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/mulberry-harbors-the-allied-secret-weapon-at-normandy/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"220\",\"title\":\"The \\\"Red Ball Express\\\" -- Army Logistics Solutions During WWII and ...\",\"description\":\"The Soldiers of the 82nd CAB have named the fixed-wing aircraft \\\"the Red Ball Express\\\" in honored remembrance of the World War II transportation solution and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.army.mil/article/77736/the_red_ball_express_army_logistics_solutions_during_wwii_and_in_afghanistan\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"221\",\"title\":\"Over-the-Shore Logistics of D-Day | The National WWII Museum\",\"description\":\"Jun 10, 2025 · In a new application of power projection, US forces provided logistical support over an unprepared beach with little infrastructure. To ...Missing:  advances liberty\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/over-shore-logistics-d-day\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"222\",\"title\":\"History - World War Two: Summary Outline of Key Events - BBC\",\"description\":\"Mar 30, 2011 · The Battle of Midway, in which US sea-based aircraft destroyed four Japanese carriers and a cruiser, marked the turning point in the Pacific War ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/history/worldwars/wwtwo/ww2_summary_01.shtml\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"223\",\"title\":\"Midway in Retrospect: The Still Under Appreciated Victory\",\"description\":\"Midway was a turning point in world history, crucial for the West, and shaped post-war Europe, despite being under-appreciated.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/research/library/online-reading-room/title-list-alphabetically/m/midway-in-retrospect-the-still-under-appreciated-victory.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"224\",\"title\":\"Battle of Midway - Naval History and Heritage Command\",\"description\":\"Against the loss of one U.S. carrier, the Japanese lost four—all of which had participated in the Pearl Harbor attack. More importantly, the Japanese lost over ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/browse-by-topic/wars-conflicts-and-operations/world-war-ii/1942/midway.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"225\",\"title\":\"Battle of Midway: 4-7 June 1942\",\"description\":\"Each side had a carrier damaged, while the American lost the carrier USS Lexington and the Japanese lost the light carrier Shoho. More important the Ja