\"\"},{\"id\":\"231\",\"title\":\"H-013-3 Operation Torch - Naval History and Heritage Command\",\"description\":\"Operation Torch was a secret invasion of French Morocco, involving 35,000 US troops, with the main objectives being Casablanca, Morocco, and Oran and Algiers, ...Missing:  outcomes | Show results with:outcomes\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/about-us/leadership/director/directors-corner/h-grams/h-gram-013/h-013-3.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"232\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Naval Aviation in Operation Torch\",\"description\":\"With all the landing forces ashore, aerial action on November 9 centered around supporting the Allied troops and ending whatever French resis- tance remained. ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/content/dam/nhhc/browse-by-topic/commemorations/commemorations-toolkits/wwii/articles-on-world-war-ii-naval-aviation/pdf/ww2-21.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"233\",\"title\":\"World War II - European-African-Middle Eastern Theater Campaigns\",\"description\":\"The British Eighth Army opened an offensive at El Alamein on 23 October 1942, after having soundly defeated a prior Axis offensive. On 8 November 1942 the U.S. ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.army.mil/Research/Reference-Topics/Army-Campaigns/Brief-Summaries/World-War-II/World-War-II-European-African-Middle-Eastern-Theater/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"234\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Northwest Africa: Seizing the Initiative In the West\",\"description\":\"Two campaigns occurred there: Operation TORCH which swiftly liberated. French North Africa ... Allied effort to destroy all the military forces of the Axis ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.army.mil/portals/143/Images/Publications/catalog/6-1.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"235\",\"title\":\"[PDF] SICILY - U.S. Army Center of Military History\",\"description\":\"On the night of 9–10 July 1943, an Allied armada of more than 3,200 vessels launched one of the largest combined operations of World War. II—the invasion of ...\"