cts | Show results with:facts\",\"url\":\"https://www.usni.org/magazines/naval-history-magazine/2018/april/turning-point-atlantic\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"241\",\"title\":\"How Alan Turing Cracked The Enigma Code | Imperial War Museums\",\"description\":\"Turing travelled to the United States in December 1942, to advise US military intelligence in the use of Bombe machines and to share his knowledge of Enigma.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/how-alan-turing-cracked-the-enigma-code\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"242\",\"title\":\"The Silent Service's Success in the Pacific - U.S. Naval Institute\",\"description\":\"A tribute at the US Naval Academy Museum overlooks the impact the submarine fleet had on destroying Japan's warships in decisive World War II battles.Missing:  disruptions | Show results with:disruptions\",\"url\":\"https://www.usni.org/magazines/proceedings/2013/june/silent-services-success-pacific\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"243\",\"title\":\"WW2 Japanese Submarines - Naval Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"A complete overview of all the types of submarines used by ww2 Japan from reconnaissance, fleet or midget types, to aircraft carriers and special types.\",\"url\":\"https://naval-encyclopedia.com/ww2/japan/submarines.php\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"244\",\"title\":\"The Reception: The Germans on D-Day | The National WWII Museum\",\"description\":\"Jun 28, 2018 · On D-Day, June 6, 1944, the German hosts botched the reception. They failed to show their unwanted guests the door, and in the end, the invaders moved in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/reception-germans-d-day\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"245\",\"title\":\"The Lies and Deceptions That Made D-Day Possible | IWM\",\"description\":\"The aim of the operation - to draw German troops away from the landing beaches - appears to have been successful, as the German army in Normandy sent a brigade ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/the-lies-and-deceptions-that-made-d-day-possible\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"246\",\"title\":\"D-Day Casualties: Operation Overlord by the Numbers\",\"description\":\"The First U.S. Army, accounting for the first twenty-four hours in Normandy, tabulated 1,465 killed, 1,928 missing, and 6,603 wounded. The after-action report ...\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/d-day-casualties-operation-overlord-by-the-numbers/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"247\",\"title\":\"Timeline: The War in Europe, After D-Day - NPR\",\"description\":\"Jun 4, 2004 · August 25, 1944: Allied troops, with the help of the French resistance led by Gen. Charles de Gaulle, liberate Paris after four years of German ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2004/06/04/1922306/timeline-the-war-in-europe-after-d-day\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"248\",\"title\":\"D-Day: The Allies Invade Europe | The National WWII Museum\",\"description\":\"Jun 6, 2024 · In May 1944, the Western Allies were finally prepared to deliver their greatest blow of the war, the long-delayed, cross-channel invasion of northern France, ...Missing:  1944-1945 | Show results with:1944-1945\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/d-day-allies-invade-europe\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"249\",\"title\":\"Battle of the Bulge | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Dec 4, 2024 · On December 16, 1944, the German army launched a massive offensive in the Ardennes Forest. The Battle of the Bulge would be the largest ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/topics/battle-bulge\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"250\",\"title\":\"Battle of the Bulge | Summary, Commanders, \u0026 Significance\",\"description\":\"Oct 3, 2025 · Battle of the Bulge, (December 16, 1944–January 16, 1945), the last major German offensive on the Western Front during World War II.\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/Battle-of-the-Bulge\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"251\",\"title\":\"Operation Undertone: The Allies Clear the Rhineland | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Mar 6, 2025 · US Third and Seventh Armies' March 1945 offensive cleared the Rhineland, pushing deep into Germany and decisively weakening German defenses ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/operation-undertone-allies-clear-rhineland\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"252\",\"title\":\"Operation Plunder: Crossing the Rhine\",\"description\":\"Feb 19, 2020 · ... Allies seemed poised to drive into Germany and end the war early in 1945. The Germans, however, launched Operation Wacht am Rhein, an ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.navy.mil/browse-by-topic/wars-conflicts-and-operations/world-war-ii/1945/operation-plunder.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"253\",\"title\":\"The Rhine Crossings in World War II - Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"The Allied crossings of the Rhine River allowed US and British troops to advance rapidly into the interior of Germany, helping to bring about the defeat of the ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/the-rhine-crossings\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"254\",\"title\":\"Operation Bagration And The Destruction Of The Army Group Center\",\"description\":\"... Operation Bagration, the Red Army offensive into Byelorussia from June 23 to August 19, 1944, resulted in the destruction of 28 of 34 divisions of the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.hoover.org/research/operation-bagration-and-destruction-army-group-center\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"255\",\"title\":\"17-Battle of the Vistula 1945 \u003e WW2 Weapons\",\"description\":\"Outcome: The offensive was a decisive Soviet victory, destroying much of Germany's remaining capacity to resist on the Eastern Front. Strategic importance: It ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.ww2-weapons.com/battle-at-the-vistula-1945/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"256\",\"title\":\"The Soviet Winter Offensive: From the Vistula to the Oder\",\"description\":\"In early January 1945 we find the Soviet armies positioned along the Vistula River to its great bend and then north along the Narew River. Stalin's armies held ...\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/the-soviet-winter-offensive-from-the-vistula-to-the-oder/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"257\",\"title\":\"The Battle of Berlin: Germany's downfall on the Eastern Front\",\"description\":\"The Battle of Berlin occurred from April 16 to May 2, 1945, with 2.5 million Soviet troops. Hitler committed suicide, and the city surrendered by May 2.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/the-battle-of-berlin-germanys-downfall-on-the-eastern-front\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"258\",\"title\":\"Battle of Berlin: Why it Became the Death Knell for Hitler's Third Reich\",\"description\":\"The rumbling was the sound of 8,983 Soviet artillery pieces, up to 270 guns every kilometer, hurling a stockpile of seven million shells (1.2 million on the ...\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/battle-of-berlin-why-it-became-the-death-knell-for-hitlers-third-reich/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"259\",\"title\":\"Battle of Berlin: The Fall of Nazi Germany\",\"description\":\"The Soviet forces led by Zhukov broke through the defensive positions after suffering about 30.000 dead, while 12.000 German personnel were killed. On April 19, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.normandy1944.info/home/battles/battle-of-berlin\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"260\",\"title\":\"The Pacific Strategy in World War II: Lessons for China's Antiaccess ...\",\"description\":\"In the final Allied planning conference of the war, it was recognized that the island-hopping campaign had provided the Allies with forward air bases that could ...Missing:  key | Show results with:key\",\"url\":\"https://www.usni.org/magazines/naval-history-magazine/2022/june/pacific-strategy-world-war-ii-lessons-chinas\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"261\",\"title\":\"Pacific Battles - Pearl Harbor National Memorial (U.S. National Park ...\",\"description\":\"Allied offensive strategy then took three broad paths: the push across the central Pacific toward the Japanese homeland with a bloody \\\"island-hopping\\\" campaign ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nps.gov/valr/learn/historyculture/pacific-battles.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"262\",\"title\":\"Iwo Jima and Okinawa: Death at Japan's Doorstep\",\"description\":\"On April 1, 1945, more than 60,000 soldiers and US Marines of the US Tenth Army stormed ashore at Okinawa, in the final island battle before an anticipated ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/iwo-jima-and-okinawa-death-japans-doorstep\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"263\",\"title\":\"Milestones: 1937–1945 - The Yalta Conference - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"Roosevelt, Churchill, and Stalin agreed not only to include France in the postwar governing of Germany, but also that Germany should assume some, but not all, ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1937-1945/yalta-conf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"264\",\"title\":\"Yalta (Crimea) Conference - The Avalon Project\",\"description\":\"The text of the agreements reached at the Crimea (Yalta) Conference between President Roosevelt, Prime Minister Churchill and Generalissimo Stalin.\",\"url\":\"https://avalon.law.yale.edu/wwii/yalta.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"265\",\"title\":\"Joint Statement with Churchill and Stalin on the Yalta Conference\",\"description\":\"We have agreed on common policies and plans for enforcing the unconditional surrender terms which we shall impose together on Nazi Germany.\",\"url\":\"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/joint-statement-with-churchill-and-stalin-the-yalta-conference\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"266\",\"title\":\"\\\"The Far East Agreements of the Yalta Conference of February 4-11 ...\",\"description\":\"This paper will present a study of the Far East Agreements of the Yalta Conference, held from February 4-11, 1945, and 