rus1945v06/ch9subsubch1\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"287\",\"title\":\"The Jewel Voice Broadcast - Atomic Heritage Foundation\",\"description\":\"On August 15, 1945, Japanese Emperor Hirohito announced the surrender of Japan to his people in the “Jewel Voice Broadcast,” or “Gyokuon-hoso.”\",\"url\":\"https://ahf.nuclearmuseum.org/ahf/key-documents/jewel-voice-broadcast/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"288\",\"title\":\"Full Circle: The Japanese Surrender in Tokyo Bay, September 2, 1945\",\"description\":\"Sep 2, 2020 · General Douglas MacArthur speaks to open the surrender ceremonies on the USS Missouri on September 2, 1945. In the background is the flag flown ...Missing:  signers | Show results with:signers\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/japanese-surrender-tokyo-bay-september-2-1945\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"289\",\"title\":\"WWII 80: The Formal Surrender of Japan - Truman Library Institute\",\"description\":\"Top: Japanese representative General Yoshijiro signs the instrument of unconditional surrender on the U.S.S. Missouri, as General Douglas MacArthur watches, ...Missing:  signers | Show results with:signers\",\"url\":\"https://www.trumanlibraryinstitute.org/wwii-80-formal-surrender-of-japan/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"290\",\"title\":\"How Many People did the Nazis Murder? | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Sep 26, 2023 · Behind the number of victims of the Holocaust and Nazi persecution are people whose hopes and dreams were destroyed. Learn about the toll of ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/documenting-numbers-of-victims-of-the-holocaust-and-nazi-persecution\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"291\",\"title\":\"The number of victims / Auschwitz and Shoah / History / Auschwitz ...\",\"description\":\"Until the end of its existence, the Auschwitz camp was above all a place of extermination. In other camps, the death rate was lowered from 1943 in an effort ...Missing:  methods | Show results with:methods\",\"url\":\"https://www.auschwitz.org/en/history/auschwitz-and-shoah/the-number-of-victims/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"292\",\"title\":\"The Nuremberg Race Laws | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Sep 25, 2025 · The Nazi regime's Nuremberg Race Laws of September 1935 made Jews legally different from their non-Jewish neighbors. The laws were the ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/the-nuremberg-race-laws\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"293\",\"title\":\"Einsatzgruppen: An Overview - Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"did not conduct these killings alone. Units of the Waffen SS ... describes roundup of Jews for mobile killing unit (Einsatzgruppen) massacre (Oral History).Missing:  Front | Show results with:Front\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/einsatzgruppen\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"294\",\"title\":\"Wannsee Conference and the \\\"Final Solution\\\"\",\"description\":\"The Wannsee Conference was a high-level meeting of German officials to discuss and implement the so-called “Final Solution of the Jewish Question” (mass ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/wannsee-conference-and-the-final-solution\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"295\",\"title\":\"The Nazi Concentration Camp System | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Apr 22, 2025 · The Nazis created at least 44000 camps, including ghettos and other sites of incarceration, between 1933 and 1945. The camps served various ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/nazi-concentration-camp-system\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"296\",\"title\":\"Polish and Slavic citizens and POWs - Holocaust Memorial Day Trust\",\"description\":\"Hundreds of thousands were also imprisoned in Nazi concentration camps. It is estimated that the Nazis killed at least 1.9 million non-Jewish Polish civilians ...\",\"url\":\"https://hmd.org.uk/learn-about-the-holocaust-and-genocides/nazi-persecution/non-jewish