80190277727.001.0001/acrefore-9780190277727-e-147\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"303\",\"title\":\"Human Experimentation at Unit 731 - Pacific Atrocities Education\",\"description\":\"Unit 731 is infamous for its human experimentation during its existence during World War 2. At least 3000 men, women, and children were subjected as ...Frostbite Picture from Unit 731 · Duties of Unit 731 · Germ Warfare Attacks · Stories\",\"url\":\"https://www.pacificatrocities.org/human-experimentation.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"304\",\"title\":\"Shedding light on Japan's WWII germ warfare program - NPR\",\"description\":\"Aug 14, 2025 · The release of WWII-era military documents this year has given a boost to researchers digging into Japan's germ warfare program.\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2025/08/14/nx-s1-5497951/japan-germ-warfare-biological-wwii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"305\",\"title\":\"United States Responses to Japanese Wartime Inhuman ...\",\"description\":\"In 1945-46, US officials made similar discoveries in both Germany and Japan, unearthing evidence of unethical experiments on human beings that constituted war ...\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4487829/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"306\",\"title\":\"Bataan Death March | Definition, Date, Pictures, Facts ... - Britannica\",\"description\":\"Oct 10, 2025 · Bataan Death March, march in the Philippines of some 66 miles that 76000 prisoners of war were forced by the Japanese military to endure in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/Bataan-Death-March\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"307\",\"title\":\"Bataan Death March: Japanese Brutality - Air Force Museum\",\"description\":\"The Bataan Death March began on April 10, 1942, when the Japanese gathered an estimated 78000 prisoners (12000 US and 66000 Filipino) to march up the east ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalmuseum.af.mil/Visit/Museum-Exhibits/Fact-Sheets/Display/Article/196797/bataan-death-march-japanese-brutality/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"308\",\"title\":\"What Life Was Like For POWs In East Asia During WW2\",\"description\":\"World War Two Prisoner of War: We look into what life was like for over 190000 British and Commonwealth Prisoners of War in the far east during WW2.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/what-life-was-like-for-pows-in-east-asia-during-the-second-world-war\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"309\",\"title\":\"Estimates Based on Facts: '200,000 Comfort Women' Defies Math\",\"description\":\"Nov 28, 2017 · Seoul National University professor emeritus of economics Lee Young-hoon has noted there were many Korean comfort station managers listed in a volume titled ...\",\"url\":\"https://japan-forward.com/estimates-based-on-facts-200000-comfort-women-defies-math/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"310\",\"title\":\"A Guide to Understanding the History of the 'Comfort Women' Issue\",\"description\":\"Sep 16, 2022 · Even before assuming office in May 2022, South Korean President Yoon Suk-yeol made clear his desire for smoother formal relations between ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.usip.org/publications/2022/09/guide-understanding-history-comfort-women-issue\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"311\",\"title\":\"The Manila Massacre: Remembering the Civilian Tragedy of 1945\",\"description\":\"Jul 15, 2025 · The Manila Massacre saw Japanese soldiers kill an ... General Tomoyuki Yamashita at the Japanese War Crimes Trials in Manila, 1945.\",\"url\":\"https://www.pacificatrocities.org/blog/the-manila-massacre-remembering-the-civilian-tragedy-of-1945\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"312\",\"title\":\"“An Orgy of Mass Murder” - Nieman Reports\",\"description\":\"Oct 30, 2018 · “An Orgy of Mass Murder”. In a new book, James M. Scott, NF '07, investigates World War II atrocities in the Philippines ... massacres of ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://niemanreports.org/an-orgy-of-mass-murder-in-a-new-book-james-m-scott-nf-07-investigates-world-war-ii-atrocities-in-the-philippines/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"313\",\"title\":\"The Soviet Massive Deportations - A Chronology - Sciences Po\",\"description\":\"1934: Josef Stalin, who had ruled the USSR with an iron hand since the end of the 1920s, launched the Great Purge in January 1934 to consolidate his power.Missing:  numbers | Show results with:numbers\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencespo.fr/mass-violence-war-massacre-resistance/fr/document/soviet-massive-deportations-chronology.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"314\",\"title\":\"The Massive Deportation of the Chechen People - Sciences Po\",\"description\":\"A. Context The Chechen deportation had a lot in common with other massive deportations carried out by the Stalinist regime. The deportation occurred during ...Context · Perpetrators · Victims · Witness\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencespo.fr/mass-violence-war-massacre-resistance/fr/document/massive-deportation-chechen-people-how-and-why-chechens-were-deported.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"315\",\"title\":\"the mass deportations of the 1940s UNHCR publication for CIS ...\",\"description\":\"May 1, 1996 · The inhabitants of the autonomous Volga German Republic were among the first to go: between 3 and 21 September 1941, 366,000 Volga Germans were ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.unhcr.org/us/publications/unhcr-publication-cis-conference-displacement-cis-punished-peoples-mass-deportations\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"316\",\"title\":\"Sürgün: The Crimean Tatars' deportation and exile - Sciences Po\",\"description\":\"A. Context Crimea is a peninsula located on the Black Sea coast in the south of today's Ukraine. Part of the peninsula's population was forced into exile in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencespo.fr/mass-violence-war-massacre-resistance/fr/document/suerguen-crimean-tatars-deportation-and-exile.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"317\",\"title\":\"[PDF] SOVIET ETHNIC CLEANSING OF THE CRIMEAN TATARS\",\"description\":\"From May. 18-20, 1944 the NKVD (People's Commissariat of Internal Affairs) loaded nearly every Crimean Tatar man, woman, and child onto train echelons bound for ...Missing:  details | Show results with:details\",\"url\":\"https://dergipark.org.tr/tr/download/article-file/700980\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"318\",\"title\":\"'There Was No Water, No Food' -- Chechens Remember Horror Of ...\",\"description\":\"Feb 22, 2014 · Seventy years ago, the entire Chechen and Ingush peoples were deported to Central Asia on the orders of Josef Stalin.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.rferl.org/a/chechen-deportation-1944-survivors/25273614.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"319\",\"title\":\"The rape of Berlin - BBC News\",\"description\":\"May 1, 2015 · But there is another story - of mass rapes by Soviet soldiers of German women in the dying days of the war. Some readers may find this story ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.com/news/magazine-32529679\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"320\",\"title\":\"Silence Broken On Red Army Rapes In Germany - NPR\",\"description\":\"Jul 17, 2009 · \\\"Before the wartime mass rape in Germany, also the German troops committed a lot of rapes mainly in Eastern Europe. And, of course, there was ...Missing:  sources | Show results with:sources\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2009/07/17/106687768/silence-broken-on-red-army-rapes-in-germany\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"321\",\"title\":\"[PDF] THE RUSSIAN RAPE OF GERMANY IN BERLIN, 1945 Krishna ...\",\"description\":\"Furthermore, these rapes can also be seen as touching on women's traditional and symbolic roles of mother, moral guide and body politic. Rape and Musculinity.\",\"url\":\"https://www.eiu.edu/historia/Thomas.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"322\",\"title\":\"RAF Bomber Command During The Second World War\",\"description\":\"The Royal Air Force's (RAF) bombing offensive against Nazi Germany was one of the longest, most expensive and controversial of the Allied campaigns during the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/raf-bomber-command-during-the-second-world-war\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"323\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The United States Strategic Bombing Surveys - Air University\",\"description\":\"The United States Strategic Bombing Survey was established by ... The heat radiation and blast actions of the. Nagasaki bomb were more intense than those of the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.airuniversity.af.edu/Portals/10/AUPress/Books/B_0020_SPANGRUD_STRATEGIC_BOMBING_SURVEYS.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"324\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The strategic bombing campaign against Germany during World War II\",\"description\":\"Survey estimates showed some 300,000 German civilians killed and 780,000 wounded. The number made homeless reached 7,500,000. 1. Allied bombing reduced the ...Missing:  credible | Show results with:credible\",\"url\":\"https://repository.lsu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=4267\u0026context=gradschool_theses\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"325\",\"title\":\"Allied bombing of Germany - Imperial War Museums\",\"description\":\"The raids destroyed 75,000 homes and around 25,000 people were killed. However at the start of the war, the bombing of civilians had been seen as unjustifiable.Missing:  statistics | Show results with:statistics\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/allied-bombing-of-germany\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"326\",\"title\":\"1945 - Bombings of Dresden - Air Force Historical Support Division\",\"description\":\"Between 13-15 February 1945, over a thousand heavy bombers of the Royal Air Force and the U.S. 8th Air Force struck the city of Dresden in eastern Germany.,\",\"url\":\"https://www.afhistory.af.mil/FAQs/Fact-Sheets/Article/458943/1945-bombings-of-dresden/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"327\",\"title\":\"Hellfire on Earth: Operation MEETINGHOUSE | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Mar 8, 2020 · The first B-29s over Tokyo were pathfinders. Coming in over the target from opposite directions, the pathfinders dropped their payload, ...Missing:  USAAF | Show results with:USAAF\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/hellfire-earth-operation-meetinghouse\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"328\",\"title\":\"[PDF] the effects of strategic bombing on german morale | aoav\",\"description\":\"The morale division of the United States Strategic Bombing Survey had as its objective, \\\"To detennine the direct and indirect effects of bombing upon the ...\",\"url\":\"https://aoav.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/The-Effects-of-Strategic-Bombing-in-WWII-on-German-Morale.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"329\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Norm of Reciprocity and the Law of Aerial Bombardment during ...\",\"description\":\"Participants in and planners of the World War II Allied bombing campaign were fully aware of the ill-formed law of war, as it related to aerial bombing. One.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://law.unimelb.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0009/3567438/Bennett.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"330\",\"title\":\"The Casablanca Conference, 1943 - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The President clearly stated, however, that the policy of unconditional surrender did not entail the destruction of the populations of the Axis powers but ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1937-1945/casablanca\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"331\",\"title\":\"CASABLANCA CONFERENCE 1943 - The Avalon Project\",\"description\":\"... Casablanca: \\\"Unconditional Surrender.\\\" In our uncompromising policy we mean no harm to the common people of the Axis nations. But we do mean to impose ...Missing:  announcement | Show results with:announcement\",\"url\":\"https://avalon.law.yale.edu/wwii/casablan.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"332\",\"title\":\"The Casablanca Conference | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Jan 27, 2023 · Thus, possibly out of frustration, Roosevelt made a surprise post-conference pronouncement to the press, calling for the “unconditional ...Missing:  announcement | Show results with:announcement\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/casablanca-conference\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"333\",\"title\":\"[395] Transcript of Press Conference - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The elimination of German, Japanese and Italian war power means the unconditional surrender by Germany, Italy, and Japan. That means a reasonable assurance of ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/historicaldocuments/frus1941-43/d395\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"334\",\"title\":\"Unconditional Surrender: Questioning FDR's Prerequisite for Peace\",\"description\":\"Marshall and Dwight D. Eisenhower figured among its critics. Eisenhower hoped to persuade both Churchill and Roosevelt to soften the policy—and German ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thehistoryreader.com/military-history/unconditional-surrender-questioning-fdrs-prerequisite-peace/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"335\",\"title\":\"Reassessing Unconditional Surrender - Chronicles Magazine\",\"description\":\"Mar 6, 2023 · The prime motive for the unconditional-surrender demand was to forestall German and Japanese claims that they had not really been beaten. The ...\",\"url\":\"https://chroniclesmagazine.org/view/reassessing-unconditional-surrender/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"336\",\"title\":\"\\\"To Bear the Unbearable\\\": Japan's Surrender, Part I | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Aug 18, 2020 · Prior to the atomic bombing of Hiroshima, Hirohito failed to intervene as the Soviet mediation effort went nowhere. Explanation for his inaction ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/japans-surrender-part-i\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"337\",\"title\":\"\\\"UNCONDITIONAL SURRENDER\\\" IN WORLD WAR II - jstor\",\"description\":\"Since the end of World War II, there have been various accounts of the \\\"unconditional surrender\\\" doctrine and assessments of its negative impact. Michael ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/45346132\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"338\",\"title\":\"Interim Committee Report - Atomic Heritage Foundation\",\"description\":\"Created by Secretary of War Henry Stimson in May of 1945, the Interim Committee provided recommendations on the use of the atomic bomb in wartime.\",\"url\":\"https://ahf.nuclearmuseum.org/ahf/key-documents/interim-committee-report-0/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"339\",\"title\":\"Operation Downfall - Proposed Invasion of Japan\",\"description\":\"The casualty rate on Okinawa was 35%; with 767,000 men scheduled to participate in taking Kyushu, it was estimated that there would be 268,000 casualties.\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/the-proposed-invasion-of-japan\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"340\",\"title\":\"Harry Truman's Decision to Use the Atomic Bomb (U.S. National ...\",\"description\":\"Jan 11, 2023 · President Truman had four options: 1) continue conventional bombing of Japanese cities; 2) invade Japan; 3) demonstrate the bomb on an unpopulated island; or, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nps.gov/articles/trumanatomicbomb.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"341\",\"title\":\"'Release When Ready' | National Archives\",\"description\":\"Feb 14, 2025 · This “release when ready” note is sometimes regarded as Truman's written approval to use the atomic bomb against Japan. Actually, it only ...Missing:  primary sources\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/publications/prologue/2005/summer/truman-atomic-bomb-telegram\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"342\",\"title\":\"Target Committee Recommendations - Atomic Heritage Foundation\",\"description\":\"A Target Committee was established on April 27, 1945, to determine the best techniques and targets in Japan to produce the most effective military destruction.\",\"url\":\"https://ahf.nuclearmuseum.org/ahf/key-documents/target-committee-recommendations/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"343\",\"title\":\"Manhattan Project: Debate Over How to Use the Bomb, 1945\",\"description\":\"On June 6, Stimson informed President Truman (right) that the Interim Committee recommended keeping the atomic bomb a secret until Japan had been bombed.\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/opennet/manhattan-project-history/Events/1945/debate.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"344\",\"title\":\"Atomic Diplomacy - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"Atomic diplomacy refers to attempts to use the threat of nuclear warfare to achieve diplomatic goals. After the first successful test of the atomic bomb in 1945 ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1945-1952/atomic\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"345\",\"title\":\"The Decision to Drop the Atomic Bomb | Harry S. Truman\",\"description\":\"This collection focuses on the decision to use the atomic bombs to end World War II with Japan. It includes documents and photographs covering the years 1945 ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.trumanlibrary.gov/library/online-collections/decision-to-drop-atomic-bomb\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"346\",\"title\":\"projected casualty - Intelligence Resource Program\",\"description\":\"Many historians use the casualty estimate that was briefed to Truman in June 1945 to claim that the projected low casualty rate of 25,000 dead did not justify ...\",\"url\":\"https://irp.fas.org/eprint/arens/chap5.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"347\",\"title\":\"Lend-Lease and Lies: The Real Story Behind Soviet Victory\",\"description\":\"The US provided $11.3 billion in Lend-Lease aid, including trucks, tanks, aircraft, and food, which Soviet leaders like Stalin said was crucial for victory.\",\"url\":\"https://usukraine.org/blog/lend-lease-and-lies-the-real-story-behind-soviet-victory\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"348\",\"title\":\"'We Would Have Lost': Did U.S. Lend-Lease Aid Tip The Balance In ...\",\"description\":\"May 7, 2020 · Under Lend-Lease, the United States provided more than one-third of all the explosives used by the Soviet Union during the war. The United ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.rferl.org/a/did-us-lend-lease-aid-tip-the-balance-in-soviet-fight-against-nazi-germany/30599486.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"349\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://nationalinterest.org/blog/buzz/lend-lease-helped-win-world-war-ii-not-eastern-front-96936\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"350\",\"title\":\"[PDF] lendlease.pdf - University of Warwick\",\"description\":\"Mark Harrison, \\\"Resource Mobilization for World War II: The USA, UK, USSR, and Germany, 1938-1945\\\", Economic History. Review, 41 (1988), 189. Page 17. - 16 -.\",\"url\":\"https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/soc/economics/staff/mharrison/public/lendlease.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"351\",\"title\":\"History - World Wars: Hitler and 'Lebensraum' in the East - BBC\",\"description\":\"Mar 30, 2011 · Between 1921 and 1925 Adolf Hitler developed the belief that Germany required Lebensraum ('living space') in order to survive.\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/history/worldwars/wwtwo/hitler_lebensraum_01.shtml\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"352\",\"title\":\"Lebensraum | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"The concept of Lebensraum, “living space,” was as a critical component in the Nazi worldview that drove both its military conquests and racial policy.\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/lebensraum\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"353\",\"title\":\"Hossbach Memorandum - The Avalon Project\",\"description\":\"For the improvement of our politico-military position our first objective, in the event of our being embroiled in war, must be to overthrow Czechoslovakia and ...\",\"url\":\"https://avalon.law.yale.edu/imt/hossbach.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"354\",\"title\":\"Triumph of Hitler: Hitler Reveals War Plans - The History Place\",\"description\":\"Hitler wanted to resolve the Lebensraum issue by 1943 to 1945 at the very latest to guard against military obsolescence, the aging of the Nazi leadership, and, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyplace.com/worldwar2/triumph/tr-hossbach.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"355\",\"title\":\"The troubling rise of Hitler revisionism - Slow Boring\",\"description\":\"Apr 14, 2025 · The take itself is hardly new. It largely recapitulates arguments that Pat Buchanan made in his 2008 book “Churchill, Hitler, and 'The Unnecessary War'.\",\"url\":\"https://www.slowboring.com/p/the-troubling-rise-of-hitler-revisionism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"356\",\"title\":\"A “good war” no more: The new World War II revisionism (Chapter 1)\",\"description\":\"Some of the revisionists have alleged that the conflict erupted not so much from aggressive German expansionism as reckless Allied interventionism. Others have ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/hi-hitler/good-war-no-more-the-new-world-war-ii-revisionism/D3012997B927768BD30BF5BCB339F593\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"357\",\"title\":\"What's the context? 31 March 1939: the British guarantee to Poland\",\"description\":\"Mar 28, 2019 · The key to the Polish guarantee was the fact that the French would fight for Poland, as they would not fight for Czechoslovakia.\",\"url\":\"https://history.blog.gov.uk/2019/03/28/whats-the-context-31-march-1939-the-british-guarantee-to-poland/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"358\",\"title\":\"How the Polish Guarantee helped provoke war - JohnDClare.net\",\"description\":\"The Polish Guarantee was the reason Britain went to war, explicitly causing the declaration of war, and was seen as the end of appeasement. It also stopped a  ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.johndclare.net/RoadtoWWII3_GuaranteeCausesWar.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"359\",\"title\":\"World War II Casualties by Country 2025 - World Population Review\",\"description\":\"The Soviet Union had the highest WWII casualties (20-27M), followed by China (15-20M), Germany (6-7.4M), and Poland (5.9-6M).\",\"url\":\"https://worldpopulationreview.com/country-rankings/world-war-two-casualties-by-country\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"360\",\"title\":\"World War Two Financial Cost | Parramatta History and Heritage\",\"description\":\"World War Two lasted 6 years and it was the most expensive war in the history. Adjusted for inflation to today's dollars, the war cost over $4 trillion.\",\"url\":\"https://historyandheritage.cityofparramatta.nsw.gov.au/research-topics/world-war-two/world-war-two-financial-cost\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"361\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Long-Term Effects of Destruction During the Second World War ...\",\"description\":\"By the end of the Second World War, an estimated 20 percent of the. West German housing stock had been destroyed. This paper examines the.\",\"url\":\"http://www.ecineq.org/wp-content/uploads/papers_EcineqLSE/EcineqLSE-69.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"362\",\"title\":\"“The Last Million:” Eastern European Displaced Persons in Postwar ...\",\"description\":\"Apr 4, 2022 · When the war ended there were approximately 11 million displaced persons (DPs) in Europe, eight million of which were located in Germany. They ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/last-million-eastern-european-displaced-persons-postwar-germany\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"363\",\"title\":\"European Refugee Movements After World War Two - BBC\",\"description\":\"Feb 17, 2011 · After WWII, millions of Germans fled or were expelled from eastern Europe, Jews sought homes, and others fled Communist regimes, with 11.5 ...Missing:  shifts | Show results with:shifts\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/history/worldwars/wwtwo/refugees_01.shtml\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"364\",\"title\":\"The Nuremberg Trial and the Tokyo War Crimes Trials (1945–1948)\",\"description\":\"Following World War II, the victorious Allied governments established the first international criminal tribunals to prosecute high-level political officials ...Missing:  primary | Show results with:primary\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1945-1952/nuremberg\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"365\",\"title\":\"The Nuremberg Trials | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"From 1945 to 1946, Nazi Germany leaders stood trial for crimes against peace, war crimes, crimes against humanity, and conspiracy to commit any of the ...Missing:  sources | Show results with:sources\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/topics/nuremberg-trials\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"366\",\"title\":\"Avalon Project - The International Military Tribunal for Germany\",\"description\":\"Reprints of the Trial of the Major War Criminals are available from the Hein Co. at 1-800-828-7571. The editing and markup of Volumes 2,12-14 was completed with ...Missing:  defendants | Show results with:defendants\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://avalon.law.yale.edu/subject_menus/imt.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"367\",\"title\":\"Verdicts of th IMT | Memorium Nuremberg Trials\",\"description\":\"The verdicts in the Major War Criminals Trial were read on September 30 and October 1, 1946. Twelve defendants were sentenced to death, three to life ...Missing:  primary sources\",\"url\":\"https://museums.nuernberg.de/memorium-nuremberg-trials/the-nuremberg-trials/the-international-military-tribunal/verdicts\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"368\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Victor's Justice: Selecting \\\"Situations\\\" at the International Criminal ...\",\"description\":\"[t]he Nuremberg and Tokyo trials have been characterized as. 'victor's justice' because only the vanquished were charged with violations of international ...\",\"url\":\"https://repository.law.uic.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1085\u0026context=lawreview\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"369\",\"title\":\"[PDF] A Note on the Nuremberg Debate - Chicago Unbound\",\"description\":\"' It has been attacked with a variety of objections: ex post facto, novelty and confusion, threat to the great traditions of Anglo-American justice, disrepute ...\",\"url\":\"https://chicagounbound.uchicago.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?referer=\u0026httpsredir=1\u0026article=11784\u0026context=journal_articles\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"370\",\"title\":\"Tokyo War Crimes Trial | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"On May 3, 1946, the prosecution opened its case charging the defendants with crimes against peace, conventional war crimes, and crimes against humanity.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/topics/tokyo-war-crimes-trial\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"371\",\"title\":\"Justice Radhabinod Pal and the Tokyo Tribunal | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"May 31, 2021 · At the Tokyo Tribunal, Justice Radhabinod Pal voted for the acquittal of all the defendants on all counts.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/justice-radhabinod-pal-tokyo-war-crimes-trial\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"372\",\"title\":\"War Crimes on Trial: The Nuremberg and Tokyo Trials | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Nov 24, 2020 · The decision to prevent Japanese Emperor Hirohito from going on trial was a part of the negotiations with Truman at Potsdam, and it affected ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/nuremberg-and-tokyo-war-crimes-trials\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"373\",\"title\":\"How the 'Big Three' Teed Up the Cold War at the 1945 Yalta ...\",\"description\":\"Jun 25, 2020 · The conference shifted Poland's borders westward, with the Soviet Union annexing much of the country's east with land seized from northeast ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/articles/yalta-conference-big-three-wwii-cold-war\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"374\",\"title\":\"Allied Occupation of Germany, 1945-52 - state.gov\",\"description\":\"The US, Great Britain, Soviet Union, and France jointly occupied Germany, dividing it into zones. The US, Britain, and France occupied West Germany, while the ...\",\"url\":\"https://2001-2009.state.gov/r/pa/ho/time/cwr/107189.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"375\",\"title\":\"Soviet expansion into Eastern Europe, 1945-1948 - BBC Bitesize\",\"description\":\"... Eastern Europe to fully fall to communism in 1948. At elections that year only communists were allowed to stand and a communist government was duly elected.\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/guides/zt8ncwx/revision/5\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"376\",\"title\":\"Stalin did not want an Iron Curtain to descend - Stanford Report\",\"description\":\"Dec 26, 2019 · Certainly after the war, Stalin saw Europe with the eyes of an ultra-realist, meaning he saw opportunities he could exploit for expansion and ...\",\"url\":\"https://news.stanford.edu/stories/2019/12/stalin-not-want-iron-curtain-descend\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"377\",\"title\":\"1945–1952: The Early Cold War - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"1945–1952: The Early Cold War. The United States emerged from World War II as one of the foremost economic, political, and military powers in the world.\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1945-1952/foreword\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"378\",\"title\":\"Iron Curtain speech (1946) | Summary, Meaning, \u0026 Significance\",\"description\":\"Sep 30, 2025 · The Iron Curtain speech was delivered by former British prime minister Winston Churchill in Fulton, Missouri, on March 5, 1946.\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Iron-Curtain-Speech\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"379\",\"title\":\"The Post War World - International Monetary Fund (IMF)\",\"description\":\"By 1945, exhausted countries faced severe economic problems that frustrated reconstruction efforts: Inflation; Debt (mostly owed to the United States); Trade ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.imf.org/external/np/exr/center/mm/eng/mm_dr_01.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"380\",\"title\":\"The German Economic Miracle Post WWII - Investopedia\",\"description\":\"Industrial output was down by a third. The country's housing stock was reduced by 20%. Food production was half the level it was before the start of the war.1 ...Missing:  facts | Show results with:facts\",\"url\":\"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/economics/09/german-economic-miracle.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"381\",\"title\":\"UN Relief and Rehabilitation Administration: \\\"A New Enterprise ...\",\"description\":\"Sep 23, 2020 · The United Nations Relief and Rehabilitation Administration saved the lives of millions of people in Europe and China from 1944-1947.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/united-nations-relief-and-rehabilitation\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"382\",\"title\":\"United Nations Relief and Rehabilitation Administration\",\"description\":\"After World War II, UNRRA sought to assist millions of refugees displaced by the war and its consequences. In the aftermath of the war, worldwide food shortages ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/united-nations-relief-and-rehabilitation-administration\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"383\",\"title\":\"Bretton Woods-GATT, 1941–1947 - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The two major accomplishments of the Bretton Woods conference were the creation of the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and the International Bank for ...Missing:  UNRRA | Show results with:UNRRA\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1937-1945/bretton-woods\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"384\",\"title\":\"Creation of the Bretton Woods System | Federal Reserve History\",\"description\":\"The Bretton Woods system was created in July 1944 by 44 nations to establish the IMF and World Bank, aiming for exchange rate stability and economic growth.Missing:  UNRRA | Show results with:UNRRA\",\"url\":\"https://www.federalreservehistory.org/essays/bretton-woods-created\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"385\",\"title\":\"Marshall Plan (1948) | National Archives\",\"description\":\"Jun 29, 2022 · The Marshall Plan, named after George Marshall, provided $13.3 billion in US aid to restore Europe's economy after WWII, signed on April 3, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/milestone-documents/marshall-plan\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"386\",\"title\":\"Marshall Plan, 1948 - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The Marshall Plan generated a resurgence of European industrialization and brought extensive investment into the region.\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1945-1952/marshall-plan\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"387\",\"title\":\"Soviet Union rejects Marshall Plan assistance | July 2, 1947\",\"description\":\"From the Soviet perspective, however, its refusal to participate in the Marshall Plan indicated its desire to remain free from American “economic imperialism” ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/july-2/soviet-union-rejects-marshall-plan-assistance\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"388\",\"title\":\"[PDF] new evidence on the soviet rejection of the marshall plan, 1947: two ...\",\"description\":\"Rather, Soviet rejection of the Marshall Plan was the natural response of a noncapitalist state trying to avoid integration into the capitalist world economy, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.wilsoncenter.org/sites/default/files/media/documents/publication/ACFB73.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"389\",\"title\":\"Publication: Lessons from the Marshall Plan\",\"description\":\"Industrial production in the recipient European countries leapt from just 87 per cent of pre-Second World War levels in 1947 to fully 135 per cent in 1951, a 55 ...\",\"url\":\"https://openknowledge.worldbank.org/entities/publication/1f656c61-d584-520b-94a3-cf7b12ae99c3\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"390\",\"title\":\"Infrastructure, Development and the Marshall Plan - UCLA Economics\",\"description\":\"Jul 1, 2020 · A back-of-the- envelope calculation shows that the Marshall Plan contributed 1.3 percentage points to Italy's 5.9 percent average annual GDP ...\",\"url\":\"https://economics.ucla.edu/infrastructure-development-and-the-marshall-plan/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"391\",\"title\":\"The Marshall Plan and Postwar Economic Recovery | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Mar 30, 2022 · The Marshall Plan was a massive commitment to European recovery after World War II that was largely supported by Americans.Missing:  facts figures\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/marshall-plan-and-postwar-economic-recovery\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"392\",\"title\":\"The Myth of the Miracle: Quantifying the Marshall Plan's Actual ...\",\"description\":\"Sep 13, 2025 · The current consensus suggests that the Marshall Plan was sufficient but not necessary for European recovery—it importantly accelerated and ...\",\"url\":\"https://explaininghistory.org/2025/09/13/the-myth-of-the-miracle-quantifying-the-marshall-plans-actual-economic-impact/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"393\",\"title\":\"Recovery and reconstruction: Europe after WWII - CEPR\",\"description\":\"Nov 21, 2019 · The struggle of Nazi Germany and Imperial Japan for global supremacy exhausted the human and economic resources of much of Europe as well as ...Missing:  facts figures\",\"url\":\"https://cepr.org/voxeu/columns/recovery-and-reconstruction-europe-after-wwii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"394\",\"title\":\"Great Responsibilities and New Global Power | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Oct 23, 2020 · World War II transformed the United States from a midlevel global power to the leader of the “free world.” With this rapid rise in power and ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/new-global-power-after-world-war-ii-1945\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"395\",\"title\":\"Decolonization of Asia and Africa, 1945–1960 - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"Between 1945 and 1960, three dozen new states in Asia and Africa achieved autonomy or outright independence from their European colonial rulers.\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1945-1952/asia-and-africa\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"396\",\"title\":\"How Did Decolonization Reshape the World? - CFR Education\",\"description\":\"Feb 14, 2023 · Economic Forces: World War II bankrupted much of Europe. · Postwar Agreements: Several countries on the losing side of World War II forfeited ...\",\"url\":\"https://education.cfr.org/learn/reading/how-did-decolonization-reshape-world\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"397\",\"title\":\"Post-1945 decolonization (Chapter 5) - Individual Rights and the ...\",\"description\":\"In the space of twenty-six years all of Europe's territorial empires collapsed, fragmenting into seventy-six new sovereign states by 1970, forty-five emerging ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/individual-rights-and-the-making-of-the-international-system/post1945-decolonization/1288760BB1630DD42D6442050313320C\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"398\",\"title\":\"The Dumbarton Oaks Conversations, 1944\",\"description\":\"Jun 15, 2017 · ... meetings took place at Dumbarton Oaks. Their outcome was the United Nations charter that was adopted in San Francisco in 1945. At these meetings ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.doaks.org/newsletter/news-archives/2015/the-dumbarton-oaks-conversations-1944\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"399\",\"title\":\"The Formation of the United Nations, 1945 - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The Founding of the UN in San Francisco ... Representatives of 50 nations met in San Francisco April-June 1945 to complete the Charter of the United Nations.\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1937-1945/un\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"400\",\"title\":\"UN Charter | United Nations\",\"description\":\"It was signed on 26 June 1945, in San Francisco, at the conclusion of the United Nations Conference on International Organization, and came into force on 24 ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.un.org/en/about-us/un-charter\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"401\",\"title\":\"United Nations Charter (1945) | National Archives\",\"description\":\"Mar 15, 2022 · On June 26, 1945, in San Francisco, the United Nations was formally established with the signing of the UN Charter. Article 111 of this ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/milestone-documents/united-nations-charter\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"402\",\"title\":\"The IMF and the World Bank\",\"description\":\"The IMF and the World Bank were created in July 1944 at an international conference in the United States (in Bretton Woods, New Hampshire) that established ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.imf.org/en/About/Factsheets/Sheets/2022/IMF-World-Bank-New\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"403\",\"title\":\"The Soviet Union and Europe after 1945 | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Even before the Germans surrendered, Soviet occupation troops assisted local Communists in installing Communist dictatorships in Romania and Bulgaria.\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/the-soviet-union-and-europe-after-1945\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"404\",\"title\":\"The Soviet takeover of Eastern Europe - BBC Bitesize\",\"description\":\"The Soviet forces moved into Germany from the East, replacing Nazi forces in a number of countries in Eastern Europe.\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zhx7nk7\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"405\",\"title\":\"In the Enemy's House: Venona and the Maturation of American ... - FBI\",\"description\":\"Oct 27, 2005 · Many young leftists in the early 1930s had entered the government in the early throes of the New Deal and embraced a Communist siren under whose ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.fbi.gov/history/history-publications-reports/in-the-enemys-house-venona-and-the-maturation-of-american-counterintelligence\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"406\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Venona: Soviet Espionage and The American Response 1939-1957\",\"description\":\"Anti-Communists suspected that some spies—perhaps including a few who were known to the US Government— remained at large. Those who criticized the ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.cia.gov/resources/csi/static/fc3235f14ff505b6f839321755cfe72d/Venona-Soviet-Espionage-and-The-American-Response-1939-1957.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"407\",\"title\":\"The Truman Doctrine, 1947 - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"At the time, the U.S. Government believed that the Soviet Union supported the Greek Communist war effort and worried that if the Communists prevailed in the ...\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1945-1952/truman-doctrine\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"408\",\"title\":\"The Truman Doctrine (1947) | The American Yawp Reader\",\"description\":\"The “Truman Doctrine” directed the United States to actively support anti-communist forces around the world.\",\"url\":\"https://www.americanyawp.com/reader/25-the-cold-war/the-truman-doctrine-1947/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"409\",\"title\":\"The Vindication of Joseph McCarthy - The Objective Standard\",\"description\":\"Nov 19, 2016 · A second is that government agencies did on occasion during this era treat as a crime the mere holding of communist views. This is evident in ...Missing:  backlash | Show results with:backlash\",\"url\":\"https://www.theobjectivestandard.com/p/vindication-joseph-mccarthy\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"410\",\"title\":\"Cold War Diplomacy\",\"description\":\"During the Cold War, US diplomacy was focused on halting the spread of communism and limiting its influence where it already existed.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://diplomacy.state.gov/discover-diplomacy/period/cold-war-diplomacy/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"411\",\"title\":\"How WWII Changed the World - American University\",\"description\":\"Sep 2, 2025 · ... communist takeovers in the decolonized nations. Hence, anti-communism took precedence over decolonization, especially under Presidents Harry ...Missing:  ideological | Show results with:ideological\",\"url\":\"https://www.american.edu/sis/news/20250902-how-wwii-changed-the-world.cfm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"412\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Communism: Its Ideology, Its History, and Its Legacy\",\"description\":\"Following World War II, Europe was the focal point for the conflict between communism and ... political party which was anti-communist, anti-. Soviet, and ...\",\"url\":\"https://victimsofcommunism.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Communism-3RD.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"413\",\"title\":\"Manhattan Project - Manhattan Project National Historical Park (U.S. ...\",\"description\":\"In just a few short years, the Manhattan Project succeeded in its mission to create the world's first atomic weapons. During this time, nuclear science advanced ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nps.gov/mapr/learn/manhattan-project.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"414\",\"title\":\"Manhattan Project Background Information and Preservation Work\",\"description\":\"The legacy of the Manhattan Project is immense. The advent of nuclear weapons not only helped bring an end to the Second World War but ushered in the atomic age ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.energy.gov/lm/manhattan-project-background-information-and-preservation-work\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"415\",\"title\":\"'Destroyer of Worlds': The Making of an Atomic Bomb | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Jul 10, 2025 · With over 30 project sites and over 100,000 workers, the Manhattan Project came to cost approximately $2.2 billion.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/making-the-atomic-bomb-trinity-test\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"416\",\"title\":\"The Discovery of Penicillin—New Insights After More Than 75 Years ...\",\"description\":\"Apr 14, 2017 · At the time, however, pharmaceutical companies in Great Britain were unable to mass produce penicillin because of World War II commitments.\",\"url\":\"https://wwwnc.cdc.gov/eid/article/23/5/16-1556_article\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"417\",\"title\":\"[PDF] “Thanks to Penicillin…He Will Come Home!”\",\"description\":\"World War II saw major advances in medical technology including the mass production of penicillin. On. March 14, 1942, U.S. made-penicillin was used to ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/sites/default/files/2017-07/thanks-to-penicillin-lesson.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"418\",\"title\":\"ENIAC - Penn Engineering\",\"description\":\"Originally announced on February 14, 1946, the Electronic Numerical Integrator and Computer (ENIAC), was the first general-purpose electronic computer.\",\"url\":\"https://www.seas.upenn.edu/about/history-heritage/eniac/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"419\",\"title\":\"The ENIAC Story\",\"description\":\"The world's first electronic digital computer was developed by Army Ordnance to compute World War II ballistic firing tables.\",\"url\":\"https://ftp.arl.army.mil/~mike/comphist/eniac-story.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"420\",\"title\":\"World War II: Overview | NIST\",\"description\":\"Science and technology assumed paramount importance during World War II, as illustrated most dramatically by the development of the atomic bomb.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nist.gov/pao/nist-100-foundations-progress/world-war-ii-overview\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"421\",\"title\":\"Women in the Work Force during World War II | National Archives\",\"description\":\"May 29, 2025 · During WWII, women took production line jobs due to men being at war, with the War Manpower Commission recruiting them. They were vital to war ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/education/lessons/wwii-women.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"422\",\"title\":\"Gender on the Home Front | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"World War II changed the lives of women and men in many ways on the Home Front. Wartime needs increased labor demands for both male and female workers.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/gender-home-front\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"423\",\"title\":\"History At a Glance: Women in World War II\",\"description\":\"Women worked in defense plants, managed households, and served in uniform in various roles, including driving trucks and repairing airplanes. Nearly 350,000 ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/students-teachers/student-resources/research-starters/women-wwii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"424\",\"title\":\"6.6 Million Women Enter the U.S. Labor Force | Research Starters\",\"description\":\"During WWII, 6.6 million women entered the U.S. labor force due to a labor shortage, working in areas like aircraft production and shipbuilding. By 1945, 18.6 ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/women-s-studies-and-feminism/66-million-women-enter-us-labor-force\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"425\",\"title\":\"Women in World War II (U.S. National Park Service)\",\"description\":\"Feb 14, 2025 · During World War II, American women entered the workforce and the military in unprecedented numbers. These dramatic changes also altered the way ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nps.gov/articles/000/women-in-world-war-ii.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"426\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Role of World War II in the Rise of Women's Employment\",\"description\":\"The 1940's were a turning point in married women's labor-force participation, leading many to credit World War II with spurring economic and social change. This ...\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.harvard.edu/sites/scholar.harvard.edu/files/goldin/files/the_role_of_world_war_ii_in_the_rise_of_womens_employment.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"427\",\"title\":\"How the Treaty of Versailles and German Guilt Led to World War II\",\"description\":\"Jun 29, 2018 · The Versailles Treaty forced Germany to give up territory to Belgium, Czechoslovakia and Poland, return Alsace and Lorraine to France and cede ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/articles/treaty-of-versailles-world-war-ii-german-guilt-effects\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"428\",\"title\":\"Historiography of the Causes of World War II - JohnDClare.net\",\"description\":\"Winston Churchill, in The Gathering Storm (1948), argued that Hitler had planned for war from the beginning, marking Hitler's rearmament in 1935 as the point ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.johndclare.net/RoadtoWWII9.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"429\",\"title\":\"AJP Taylor's Origins of the Second World War - Paradox Forum\",\"description\":\"Mar 10, 2012 · Taylor argued that the basic problem with an interwar Europe was a flawed Treaty of Versailles that was sufficiently onerous to ensure that the ...\",\"url\":\"https://forum.paradoxplaza.com/forum/threads/ajp-taylors-origins-of-the-second-world-war.594029/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"430\",\"title\":\"A. J. P. Taylor and the Nuremberg Thesis | by Nick Nielsen | Medium\",\"description\":\"Apr 19, 2025 · Both of these books stirred up renewed debate about the Second World War, and both could be considered revisionist historiography. We often hear ...Missing:  II | Show results with:II\",\"url\":\"https://jnnielsen.medium.com/a-j-p-taylor-and-the-nuremberg-thesis-85f2286e06a5\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"431\",\"title\":\"The Forced War: Hoggan, David L - Amazon.com\",\"description\":\"30-day returnsDavid Hoggan explains why Hitler decided to attack Poland in 1939 and examines the shortsighted policies that made war all but inevitable. He examines the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.amazon.com/Forced-War-David-L-Hoggan/dp/0939484811\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"432\",\"title\":\"World War II - historical view - Articles Institute of National ...\",\"description\":\"Mar 14, 2021 · In May 1939 in no uncertain terms Poland rejected German territorial demands. World War II - historical view. I. POLITICAL SITUATION IN ...\",\"url\":\"https://eng.ipn.gov.pl/en/digital-resources/articles/7781%2CWorld-War-II-historical-view.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"433\",\"title\":\"Lies About the Holocaust - Commentary Magazine\",\"description\":\"Dec 1, 1980 · The first—and still the only—revisionist work on World War II by a reputable historian was A.J.P. Taylor's mischievous book, The Origins of the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.commentary.org/articles/lucy-dawidowicz/lies-about-the-holocaust/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"434\",\"title\":\"[PDF] HISTORIOGRAPHY CAUSES OF WWII - IB History.\",\"description\":\"Nov 11, 2018 · Revisionist view: Most revisionists reject the idea of Hitler being an all-powerful leader in complete control of events. They portray him ...\",\"url\":\"https://grudichistory.weebly.com/uploads/4/9/4/3/49437683/historiography_causes_of_ww2.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"435\",\"title\":\"What Motivated Japanese Aggression in World War II? - ThoughtCo\",\"description\":\"May 1, 2025 · Japan's fear of outside aggression stemmed in large part from its experience with western imperial powers, beginning with the arrival of ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thoughtco.com/japanese-aggression-in-world-war-ii-195806\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"436\",\"title\":\"The Great Debate | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"The Japanese attack on Pearl Harbor on December 7, 1941, ended the debate over American intervention in both the Pacific and European theaters of World War II.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/great-debate\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"437\",\"title\":\"American Entry into World War II: A Historiographical Appraisal - jstor\",\"description\":\"The aggressive expansion of the Axis powers in Europe and Asia in the 1930's aroused an impassioned debate on American foreign policy. \\\"Isolationists ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/1902275\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"438\",\"title\":\"The Origins of the Second World War, by A. J. P. Taylor\",\"description\":\"Taylor claims that Hitler always wanted to avoid war, although he was ready to threaten it in order to get his way, and that he did not really want territorial ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.commentary.org/articles/g-hudson/the-origins-of-the-second-world-war-by-a-j-p-taylor/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"439\",\"title\":\"The origins of the Second World War - The Montreal Review\",\"description\":\"Taylor's most popular conclusion in \\\"The Origins of The Second World War\\\" is that Hitler had no real plan for German expansion.\",\"url\":\"https://www.themontrealreview.com/2009/The-origins-of-the-Second-World-War.php\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"440\",\"title\":\"The Origins of the Second World War by A J P Taylor: a Military ...\",\"description\":\"Jan 10, 2011 · Taylor's point is that the Second World War was, in some sense, caused by the 'international anarchy' of a world divided between great powers; ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.military-history.org/books/the-origins-of-the-second-world-war-by-a-j-p-taylor-a-military-times-classic.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"441\",\"title\":\"(PDF) The Case for Pearl Harbor Revisionism - Academia.edu\",\"description\":\"Revisionists argue that, instead of following an aggressive plan of conquest, Japanese moves were fundamentally defensive efforts to protect vital Japanese ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/20230947/The_Case_for_Pearl_Harbor_Revisionism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"442\",\"title\":\"Did Economics Cause World War II? | NBER\",\"description\":\"Dec 11, 2008 · Historians have long recognized the role of economic resources and organization in determining the outcome of World War II: the Nazi economy ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nber.org/papers/w14560\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"443\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The economics of World War II: an overview* - University of Warwick\",\"description\":\"Introduction: economic factors in the war. This book deals with two issues in the economics of twentieth century warfare. First is the contribution of ...\",\"url\":\"https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/soc/economics/staff/mharrison/public/ww2overview1998.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"444\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Global Trade Contraction: How Much is 2008-09 Like 1929-33?\",\"description\":\"In 1929-33, global exports declined 64%, US exports 66%. In 2008-09, imports fell 36%, exports 35%. Both periods had similar factors, but trade is more ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.usitc.gov/publications/332/TradeandRecessionExecutiveBriefing.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"445\",\"title\":\"Unemployment in Interwar Germany: An Analysis of the Labor ...\",\"description\":\"Sep 8, 2006 · Between the summer of 1929 and early 1932, German unemployment rose from just under 1.3 million to over 6 million, corresponding to a rise in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/journal-of-economic-history/article/unemployment-in-interwar-germany-an-analysis-of-the-labor-market-19271936/A4917F1EBC8DB5D5A98655E005C4CD06\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"446\",\"title\":\"Great Depression | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"The Great Depression was a contributing factor to dire economic conditions in Weimar Germany which led in part to the rise of Adolf Hitler and the Nazi Party.\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/the-great-depression\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"447\",\"title\":\"How Economic Conditions Contributed to World War II - Investopedia\",\"description\":\"Sep 27, 2023 · The combination of a poorly designed peace treaty and a global economic crisis in the modern world culminated in conditions ripe for World War II.\",\"url\":\"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/markets/022516/economic-conditions-helped-cause-world-war-ii.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"448\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Economics of the Second World War: Seventy-Five Years On\",\"description\":\"The Soviet economy and war preparations. Mark Harrison. 29. Putin ... Lend-Lease administration did not predict and could not control the Soviet economy's.\",\"url\":\"https://cepr.org/system/files/publication-files/60043-the_economics_of_the_second_world_war_seventy_five_years_on.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"449\",\"title\":\"The Venona Project - HistoryNet\",\"description\":\"Mar 10, 2020 · The release of the Venona intercepts answered many questions regarding the immense Soviet penetration of the U.S. government during and after ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.historynet.com/the-venona-project/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"450\",\"title\":\"Opening the Venona Files - Warfare History Network\",\"description\":\"Jun 9, 2024 · The Venona Project gives the modern-day historian a clearer view of just how much our wartime Soviet ally penetrated the US government.\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/opening-the-venona-files/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"451\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Venona S tory - National Security Agency\",\"description\":\"That release was a compilation of forty-nine VENONA translations which related to Soviet espionage efforts against U.S. atomic bomb research, including messages ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nsa.gov/portals/75/documents/about/cryptologic-heritage/historical-figures-publications/publications/coldwar/venona_story.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"452\",\"title\":\"[PDF] DOCID: 3674579 SIGINT and the Holocaust\",\"description\":\"They described in amazing detail what was going on at Auschwitz; they named the SS officers in charge, described the layout of the camps and ofthe gas chambers.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nsa.gov/portals/75/documents/news-features/declassified-documents/cryptologic-quarterly/sigint_and_the_holocaust.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"453\",\"title\":\"Newly Declassified OSS Records Shed New Light on World War II\",\"description\":\"Jun 26, 2000 · The messages provide historical insight into what the Allied governments knew about the Holocaust, when they learned it, and what might have ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/press/press-releases/2000/nr00-85\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"454\",\"title\":\"Holocaust files reveal Allies' knowledge – DW – 04/19/2017\",\"description\":\"Apr 19, 2017 · The UN War Crimes Commission has finally released files that show the Allies knew much more about the Holocaust during WWII than previously thought.\",\"url\":\"https://www.dw.com/en/un-holocaust-files-reveal-allies-knowledge/a-38498671\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"455\",\"title\":\"Thousands of Intelligence Documents Opened under the Nazi War ...\",\"description\":\"May 13, 2004 · The latest release of records, when combined with previously available documents, alter our understanding of certain aspects of the Holocaust.\",\"url\":\"https://www.archives.gov/press/press-releases/2004/nr04-55\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"456\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Operation Paperclip: The Secret Intelligence Program to Bring Nazi ...\",\"description\":\"Operation Paperclip, by. Annie Jacobsen, provides perhaps the most comprehen- sive, up-to-date narrative available to the general public. Her book is a detailed ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cia.gov/resources/csi/static/Review-Operation-Paperclip.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"457\",\"title\":\"Operation Paperclip - Defense Media Network\",\"description\":\"Jan 8, 2021 · Operation Paperclip was a special operation to bring German scientists and technologies to the US, named after the paperclips on their files.\",\"url\":\"https://www.defensemedianetwork.com/stories/operation-paperclip-a-deal-with-the-devil/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"458\",\"title\":\"A Nazi document trove raises questions for Argentina - Reuters\",\"description\":\"Jul 15, 2025 · The court had found a dozen boxes of Nazi documents in its basement archive containing photos of Hitler as well as thousands of red Nazi labor organization ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/nazi-document-trove-raises-questions-argentina-2025-07-15/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"459\",\"title\":\"Argentina To Declassify Archives On Nazis Who Took Refuge After ...\",\"description\":\"Mar 27, 2025 · Argentinian President Javier Milei announced the declassification of significant archival documents revealing the identities of the Nazis who fled to Argentina.\",\"url\":\"https://www.i24news.tv/en/news/international/latin-america/artc-argentina-to-declassify-archives-on-nazis-who-took-refuge-after-world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"460\",\"title\":\"The Atomic Bombings of Japan and the End of World War II, 80 ...\",\"description\":\"Aug 5, 2025 · Eighty years later, Hiroshima and Nagasaki remain emblematic of the dangers and human costs of warfare, specifically the use of nuclear weapons ...Missing:  endgame | Show results with:endgame\",\"url\":\"https://nsarchive.gwu.edu/briefing-book/nuclear-vault/2025-08-05/atomic-bombings-japan-and-end-world-war-ii-80-years-later\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"461\",\"title\":\"The Atomic Bomb and the End of World War II\",\"description\":\"Aug 4, 2020 · The bombings were the first time that nuclear weapons had been detonated in combat operations. They caused terrible human losses and destruction.\",\"url\":\"https://nsarchive.gwu.edu/briefing-book/nuclear-vault/2020-08-04/atomic-bomb-end-world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"462\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Truman's Atomic Bomb Decision. An Attack on Japan's Center of ...\",\"description\":\"Truman's decision to use the atomic bomb was to end the war, targeting Japan's leadership, and to send a message to the Soviet Union.\",\"url\":\"https://apps.dtic.mil/sti/tr/pdf/ADA308515.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"}],\"images\":[],\"fixedIssues\":[],\"slug\":\"World_War_II\",\"title\":\"World War II\",\"content\":\"$14\",\"description\":\"World War II\\n\\nWorld War II (1939–1945) was a total war involving the majority of the world's nations, including all major powers, arrayed in two opposing military coalitions: the Allies, led by the...\",\"metadata\":{\"categories\":[\"WWII\",\"WW2\",\"World War 2\",\"World War Two\",\"The Second World War\",\"Second World War\"],\"lastModified\":\"1761583892\",\"contentLength\":\"264431\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"lastEditor\":\"system\",\"language\":\"en\",\"isRedirect\":false,\"redirectTarget\":\"\",\"isWithheld\":false},\"stats\":{\"totalViews\":\"9994366\",\"recentViews\":\"9994366\",\"dailyAvgViews\":333145.53125,\"qualityScore\":1,\"lastViewed\":\"1761654057\"},\"linkedPages\":null},\"found\":true},\"dataUpdateCount\":1,\"dataUpdatedAt\":1761654057920,\"error\":null,\"errorUpdateCount\":0,\"errorUpdatedAt\":0,\"fetchFailureCount\":0,\"fetchFailureReason\":null,\"fetchMeta\":null,\"isInvalidated\":false,\"status\":\"success\",\"fetchStatus\":\"idle\"},\"queryKey\":[\"page\",\"World_War_II\"],\"queryHash\":\"[\\\"page\\\",\\\"World_War_II\\\"]\"}]},\"children\":\"$L15\"}]\n"])</script><script nonce="YTMwNDI1OWEtMGExNi00OWQyLWIzZWEtNzQ2NTg3YWE3Njdm">self.__next_f.push([1,"c:{\"metadata\":[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"World War II | Grokipedia\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"World War II (1939–1945) was a total war involving the majority of the world's nations, including all major powers, arrayed in two opposing military coalitions: the Allies, led by the United Kingdom, the Soviet Union, the United States, and China, and the Axis powers, principally Nazi Germany, Fascist Italy, and Imperial Japan. The conflict arose from unresolved grievances of the Treaty of Versailles, economic depression fueling authoritarian regimes, and aggressive territorial expansions by...\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"2\",{\"name\":\"author\",\"content\":\"system\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"3\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/manifest.webmanifest\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"keywords\",\"content\":\"WWII, WW2, World War 2, World War Two, The Second World War, Second World War\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"name\":\"googlebot\",\"content\":\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"7\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://grokipedia.com/page/World_War_II\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"prop